[Prop EHI:p:h1(x)=h1(-x) of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying (equation EHI:e:regularJumps of the paper). Suppose $B(0, r) \Subset D$, and let $h$ be a function that is non-negative everywhere and harmonic on $D$. Suppose $r_0 \geq r/L$ for some $L>1$. Then there exists a universal constant $C_{(EHI:p:h1(x)=h1(-x) of the paper)}(L, c_j)$ (depending on $L$ and $c_j$) such that for all $x \in B(0, r)$,
    \begin{equation*}
        C_{(EHI:p:h1(x)=h1(-x) of the paper)}(L, c_j)^{-1} h^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle, >0}_{B(0, r)}(-x) \leq h^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle, >0}_{B(0, r)}(x) \leq C_{(EHI:p:h1(x)=h1(-x) of the paper)}(L, c_j) h^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle, >0}_{B(0, r)}(-x). 
    \end{equation*}

