[Lemma lemma_densitygeneralfunctional of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Let $F\in \mathcal{A}$ and $a$ be a real-valued function such that $\Gamma\brac{F,-L^{-1}a(F)}^{-1}\in L^{4}(E,\mu)$. Set $h_F:= \Gamma\brac{F,-L^{-1}2a(F)}$. Then $F$ admits a density with the representation
\begin{align*}
   p_F(x)=  \E{\mathds{1}_{\{F>x\}}\brac{\frac{-2\mathbb{E}{\left[ a(F)\right]}+2a(F)}{h_F}+\frac{\Gamma\brac{-L^{-1}2a(F),h_F }}{h_F^2}}  }. 
\end{align*}

