[Definition def:path_sol_MKV of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $(W,(\mathcal{F}_t)_t)$ be a Brownian motion and \textcolor{black}{$\xi\in m\mathcal{F}_0$}. A (pathwise) solution to MKV$({\bf b},{\boldsymbol\sigma};\textcolor{black}{ \xi, W, (\mathcal{F}_t)_t})$ 
is a 
process $X$ such that the triple $(\textcolor{black}{W}, (\mathcal{F}_t)_t, X)$ 
is a (general) solution to MKV$({\bf b},{\boldsymbol\sigma})$ with 
\begin{equation}
\textcolor{black}{X_0 = \xi}. \vspace{-10pt}
\end{equation}

[Lem 9 of arXiv:2609.01101, '2609.01101'] There exist constants $A_2\ge1$ and $\eta_0\ge1$, depending only on
the fixed fields and on $\mathbf a$, such that the following
holds.  Let $\eta\ge\eta_0$ be fixed, and suppose that $T$ is sufficiently
large in terms of $\eta$.  Set
\begin{equation}
N=T^{1/2},\qquad \gamma=\frac12+\frac{\eta}{\log T}.
\end{equation}
Then, uniformly for $|b_i|\le T/2$,
\begin{align}
\sum_{n\le N}\frac{|c_{\mathbf b}(n)|^2}{n^{2\gamma}}
&\gg \eta^{-A_2}B(T,\mathbf b,\mathbf a), \\
\sum_{n\le N}\frac{|c_{\mathbf b}(n)|^2}{n}
&\ll B(T,\mathbf b,\mathbf a).                 
\end{align}

