[Defn 96 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Let $k \in \mathbb N$ and $1\leq i\neq j \leq k$. Consider a decreasing function $F:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ of exponential decay at infinity. We define the functional $V^{ij}(F;\bullet):(I^k)^{\mathbb Z_{\ge 0}} \to I^{\mathbb Z_{\ge 0}}$ by 
  \begin{align}

      V^{ij}(F;r):= \sum_{s=0}^{r-1} F(|   R^i_{s}-   R^j_{s}|).
  \end{align}
We remark that the processes $V^{ij}(F;\bullet)$ are predictable with respect to the canonical filtration on $(I^k)^{\mathbb Z_{\ge 0}}$.

