[Proposition prop: limits of integrals involving r of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] The following property holds in the set $\Gamma$ of probability one:
	\begin{equation*}
		\lim_{N \to \infty} \angled{\phi \bar r\left(\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_t^N\right)}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_t^N} = \angled{\phi \bar r\left(\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_t\right)}{\bar\boldsymbol{\mu}_t} \quad \text{for all} \quad \phi \in C_b\left(\mathbbm{R}_+^2\right) \quad \text{and} \quad t \in \mathcal{C}.
	\end{equation*}

