[Theorem thm:qf-unbounded of arXiv:2603.07132, 'Quadratic form of heavy-tailed self-normalized random vector with applications in $\alpha$'] Let $Q_{n,1}$ be as defined in (equation Def-Qn1Qn2 of the paper) and $\alpha\in (0,2)$. Assume that $\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n\delta_{a_{ii}^{(n)}}$ converges weakly almost surely to a deterministic probability measure $\nu$ and that 
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\limsup_{n\rightarrow\infty}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n|a_{ii}^{(n)}|\1(|a_{ii}^{(n)}|>T)=0 \qquad {\rm a.s.}
	\end{equation}
	Then $Q_{n,1}$ converges in distribution to a random variable with induced probability measure $\mu_{\nu,\alpha}$ whose Stieltjes transform is given by (equation Eq-Stieltjes-transform-Quadratic-form of the paper).

