[Proposition 5 (Two-point decomposition) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] For every $\nu\in \mathcal{M}(1)$, there exists a probability measure $\eta_\nu$ on $\Theta$ such that
\begin{equation}
\nu(A) = \int_\Theta Q_\theta(A)\,\eta_\nu(\dd\theta).

\end{equation}
$A\subseteq[0,\infty)$ is Borel.

