\begin{align}   
    T_J[q(d^{\uparrow}_J)](x) & = \int_0^1 J(x, y) q(d^{\uparrow}_J(y)) \mathrm d y \nonumber \\ 
    & = \frac{1}{2} \int_{-a}^a \operatorname{sgn}( d_J^{\uparrow}(x) - t)q(t) \mathrm{d} t  \nonumber \\ 
    & = \mathbb{E} [a \operatorname{sgn}( d_J^{\uparrow}(x) - d_J^{\uparrow}(\eta))q(d_J^{\uparrow}(\eta)) ] ,  
    \end{align}  
where $\eta \sim \mathrm{Unif}([0,1])$. The first equality in  (equation eq:polynomialIdentity of the paper) is from the definition of $T_J$ and the third equality is because $d_J^{\uparrow}(\eta)\sim \mathrm{Unif}([-a,a])$ (by Lemma (lm:TJr of the paper)). Also, note that it suffices to verify the ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:6625b0a7f8082950f96e9c5b8cb3c7c50f7157d462d2537f186082d62b28f072","revision_digest":"sha256:c7c1e6ea12d87841142093c52f6e1e615f379b53e54c2ea94ee52ece6a7778f3","source_id":"arxiv:2606.02340","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

