[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2511.05386, 'CLT for $\beta$-ensembles with Freud weights, application to the KLS conjecture in Schatte'] Let $p>2$. 
		Let $\delta_0$, $\cR$ and $\cT$ be as in Lemma \ref{lem:stability}. 
		Then there exists $C>0$ such that the following holds, for any $N \geq 1$ and $\alpha\in[0,1]$.
		Assume that there exist $a\geq 1$ and $B_N \colon \cR \to (0,\infty)$ such that, for any $z \in \cR$ and $q \geq 1$,
		\begin{equation} 
			\E_\alpha\left[\abs{L_N(f_{\alpha,z})}^q\right] \leq (q^aB_N(z))^q.
		\end{equation}
		Let $B_{\max} \coloneqq 1 \vee \sup_{z \in \overline{\cR \setminus \cT}} B_N(z)$.
		Then, for any $q \geq 1$,
		\begin{equation}
			\E_\alpha\left[\mathcal{N}([1,\infty))^{q}\right]
			\leq (Cq)^{2aq} B_{\max}^{2q}.
		\end{equation}

