[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2605.14254, '2605.14254'] Let $X$ be a Feller process with arbitrary initial distribution, and fix any optional time $\tau$. Then these conditions are equivalent:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[(i)] $\tau$ is predictable;
			\item[(ii)] $\tau$ is accessible;
			\item[(iii)]$X_{\tau-}=X_\tau$ a.s. on $\{\tau<\infty\}$.
		\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:widetilde_gammas of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] Let  $i,j\subset \{1,\dots,n\}$, $\zeta>0$ and $\epsilon<1$. Under {\bf Assumption 1} given in (equation Ass1 of the paper), we have: 
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{E}_\epsilon [\widetilde\gamma_{0}^{\epsilon}(i,j,\lambda, t-\lambda)]\lesssim \frac{\epsilon^{1-3\zeta}}{\lambda^{1-\zeta}}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{E}_\epsilon [\widetilde\gamma^\epsilon_{2}(i,j,\lambda, t-\lambda)]\lesssim \frac{\epsilon^{3/2-2\zeta}}{\lambda^{1-\zeta}}.
\end{equation}
For any $J\subset\{1,\dots,n\}$ and $1\leq p\leq n$,
               \begin{equation}
  \mathbf{E}_\epsilon [ \widetilde\gamma^\epsilon_{p}(\lambda)]\lesssim \psi_{p+1}^\epsilon(\lambda).
  \end{equation}

