[Lem ratesHaarU of arXiv:2412.00593, 'A new approach to strong convergence II.\\The classical ensembles'] There exists a linear functional $\mu_m$ on $\mathcal{P}$ for every $m\in\mathbb{Z}_+$ 
such that for every $q\in\mathbb{N}$ and $h\in \mathcal{P}_q$
\begin{equation}

	|\mu_m(h)| 
	\le 
	\bigg(
	(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^m
	+\frac{(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^{2m}}{m!} 
	\bigg)
	\sobnorm{h}{0}{[-K, K]},
\end{equation}
and such that for all $N\in\mathbb{N}$
\begin{equation}

	\left| \mathbf{E}[\mathop{\textnormal{tr}} h(X^N)]- \sum_{k=0}^{m-1} \frac{\mu_k(h)}{N^k} 
	\right| \leq 
	\frac{1}{N^m}
	\bigg(
	(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^m
	+\frac{(C\tilde q\tilde q_0)^{2m}}{m!} 
	\bigg)
	\sobnorm{h}{0}{[-K, K]}.
\end{equation}
Here $C$ is a universal constant,
$\tilde q:=q(1+\log q)$, and $\tilde q_0:=q_0(1+\log q_0)$.

[Lem bulk-KR of arXiv:2606.09712, 'Nearest zero-critical point distances for Gaussian SU(2) polynomials'] Let $R>1$ be fixed. Let \(I\) be uniformly distributed on \(\{1,\ldots,n\}\), independently of
\(p_n\), and let \(z_I\) be the corresponding zero.  Condition on the event
\(z_I\in K_R\).  Let
\(\beta_I\) be the nearest critical point to \(z_I\) in
Fubini--Study distance.  Then, in the affine coordinate, we have \begin{equation}
        n(\beta_I-z_I)
        +\frac 1{ V_{\mathrm{FS}}(z_I)}\to 0

\end{equation}
in probability, conditionally on \(z_I\in K_R\).  Consequently, the Fubini--Study distance satisfies 
\begin{equation}
        nD_n(z_I)-\frac2{|z_I|}\to 0
\end{equation}
in probability, conditionally on \(z_I\in K_R\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.13235, 'Mixing Properties of Random Laguerre Tessellations'] Let $\ppp$ be a stationary marked point process on $\rd \times \R$ such that it is \as non-empty. Then for any $x \in \rd$ and any $a > 0$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{r \rightarrow \infty}\p(\ppp(B(rx,ra) \times (-\infty,r^2])=0) =0. 
    \end{equation*}

