[Lemma lem: Decorrelation of bad events of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] For small enough $\beta$, there exists $C>0$ such that for any $c_1\in (0,\frac{1}{3})$ and $c_2\in (0,1)$, for any $u,v\in V$,
    \begin{equation*}
        |\text{Cov}(u,v)|\leq Ce^{-c d(u,v)}
    \end{equation*}
    where we recall that $d(u,v)$ is the graph distance on the tree and 
    \begin{equation*}
        e^{-c}:=\max\{e^{-c_1\lambda(\beta)},|\lambda_2(P_A)|^{\frac{c_2}{6}}\}
    \end{equation*}
    where $\lambda(\beta)$ is defined in Lemma (lem: Key Lemma of the paper) and $\lambda_2(P_A)$ is the second largest eigenvalue (in modulus) of the transition matrix $P_A$ of $\mu_A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:I:minus:beta:larger of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] Assume $x_0 = \Theta(1)$ and $K=\Theta((\log m)^{1/4})$. For $\beta > x_0$, we have that conditioning on $A_\epsilon$ with $\epsilon \in (0,1)$,
\begin{align*}
    \Big| 
        \mfrac{ \log I_-}{x_0 \beta \log m - \frac{x_0^2}{2} \log m  } 
        \,-\, 
        1
    \Big|
    \;=&\;
    O\Big( 
        \mfrac{\epsilon}{(1-\epsilon)\log m}
        +
        \mfrac{1}{(\log m)^{1/4}}
    \Big)
    \;.
\end{align*}

