[Lemma lem:C of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] For $d>2$, there are contants $a_0 > 0$ and $a_1 \in (0,1)$ such that for all $\mu \in (0, 1]$,
\begin{align}

C_\mu(x) \le \frac{ a_0 }{ \nnnorm x^{d-2} } e^{-a_1 m_0(\mu) \norm x _ \infty}
	\qquad(x\in \mathbb Z^d).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 22 of arXiv:2606.13459, 'Symmetric Cooperative Motion in Higher Dimensions'] Let $\Ga \in (0, \sfrac{1}{3})$, and any $R\in [(2d\ga)^{-1}, \infty)$ where $\ga=\ga(d,m)$ is defined near \eqref{hformula}. For $\mathcal{O}$ as defined in \eqref{e.regdefs} and $\mathcal{S}$ as defined in \eqref{e.bbSdef},
\begin{equation*}
\sum_{(k,n)\in \mathcal{O}} (\bar{u}_{n+1}(k)-\mathcal{S}\bar{u}_{n}(k))_{+}=0.
\end{equation*}

