[Prop CM LT of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] For all sufficiently small $r > 0$,
  we have the following.
  For any $x_0 \in M$ and $\eta \in (0, \infty)$, it holds that
  \begin{equation}
    \frac{1}{\mu(B(x_0,r))}
    \int_{B(x_0,r)}
    \hat{P}_{\diag(x)}\!
    \left(
      \Pi_{r^{d^{\mathrm{min}}_\mathrm{w}}}(B(x, 2r)) < \eta r^{d^{\mathrm{min}}_\mathrm{w}d_{\mathrm{ct}}}
    \right)
    \mu(dx)
    \leq \tilde{c} \eta.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop comparison-with-p2 of arXiv:2609.03856, 'Consensus time for asynchronous $\ell^p$ relaxation: graph dependence'] For every finite connected graph and every $2\le p<\infty$,
\[
  \lambda_p(G)\ge c_p\lambda_2(G).
\]
Moreover, for $0<\varepsilon\le1$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathsf T_p(G,\varepsilon)
  \le C_p\frac{n}{\lambda_2(G)}
       \log\!\left(\frac{en}{\varepsilon}\right).

\end{equation}

