[Lemma lem:graphic of arXiv:2609.01672, '\textbf{All-Minors Matrix-Tree Theory for Superport Networks:\\ Completed Quotient-Inciden'] For every spanning forest \(F\), every square minor of \(B_F\) belongs to \(\{0,+1,-1\}\). In particular, if \(|S|=s-1\),
\begin{equation}
\chi_F(S)\in\{0,+1,-1\},
\end{equation}
and \(\chi_F(S)\neq0\) if and only if the quotient edges in \(S\) form a spanning tree of \(H_F\).

