[Lemma lem:regularity of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Fix $\theta>0$.  There is $C_\theta<\infty$ such that for every unit vector $y\in\mathbb{R}^n$ there is $J\subseteq[n]$ with $|J|\le C_\theta d\log d$ for which, writing $r=\|y_{J^c}\|_2$, one of the following holds:
\begin{align}
&r\le d^{-2};\\
&r>0\quad\text{and}\quad \left\|\frac{y_{J^c}}r\right\|_\infty \le\frac{\theta}{\sqrt d}.

\end{align}

