[Lemma lem: lemma B1 from 8 of arXiv:2601.05361, 'Noise sensitivity in last-passage percolation'] Let $(\omega_x)_{x\in{\mathbb{Z}}^2}$ and $(\tilde\omega_x)_{x\in{\mathbb{Z}}^2}$ be two collection of (deterministic) weights satisfying the relation $\omega_{i\mathbf{e}_1}\ge\tilde\omega_{i\mathbf{e}_1}$ and $\omega_{i\mathbf{e}_2}\le\tilde\omega_{i\mathbf{e}_2}$ for $i\ge0$, and $\omega_x=\tilde\omega_x$ for $x\ge \mathbf{e}_+$.

    Let $T(0,x)$ and $\tilde{T}(0, x)$ denote the travel time between the origin and $x$ with respect to $\omega$ and $\tilde\omega$, respectively. Then, for all $x\in{\mathbb{Z}}^2_{\geq 0}$ we have
    \begin{eqnarray*}
    \tilde{T}(0, x+\mathbf{e}_2)-\tilde{T}(0, x)\geq T(0, x+\mathbf{e}_2)-T(0, x);\\
    \tilde{T}(0, x+\mathbf{e}_1)-\tilde{T}(0, x)\leq T(0, x+\mathbf{e}_1)-T(0, x).
    \end{eqnarray*}

[Lem symGen of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] Let $M$ be a generator of an irreducible Markov chain on a finite state space $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ and $\zeta\in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$. 
    The symmetrised generator $M^\zeta$~(equation eq:symGen of the paper) is irreducible and is reversible with respect to its steady state $\zeta$. Consequently, $\zeta$ satisfies the PI and the standard LSI, i.e., 
    \begin{equation}
        \forall f\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}_{>0}: \ \ \operatorname{var}_\zeta(f)\leq \frac{1}{\lambda_{\zeta}}\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f,M^\zeta), \ \ \mathrm{Ent}_\zeta(f^2) \leq \frac{1}{\alpha_{\sLSI} (M^\zeta)}\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f,M^\zeta),
    \end{equation}
    where $\mathrm{Ent}_\zeta(\cdot)$ is the centred entropy~(equation eq:CentEnt of the paper),  $\mathscr{E}_\zeta(\cdot,M^\zeta)$ is the Dirichlet form using the generator $M^\zeta$, and $\lambda_{\zeta} = \alpha_{\PI}(M^\zeta) = \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta, M) > 0$ is the spectral gap for the generator $-M^\zeta$. Furthermore, we have the relation
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\lambda_{\zeta}}{2+\log\dfrac{1}{\zeta_*}}\leq \alpha_{\sLSI}(M^\zeta) \leq 2\lambda_{\zeta},
    \end{equation}
    where $\zeta_*=\min_z\zeta(z)$.

