[Lemma Y N is open of arXiv:2609.04072, 'Oort's conjecture for split unitary Shimura varieties'] The set of $\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p$-points
    \begin{equation}
        Y_{\Lambda_0}(\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p)=\{M\in \mathcal{C}_{\Lambda_0}(\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p) \mid \operatorname{Aut}(M,F)=\Gamma_{\operatorname{gen}}\}
    \end{equation}
    defines an open subscheme $Y_{\Lambda_0}$ of $\mathcal C_{\Lambda_0}$. 

    Moreover it is dense in $\mathcal C_{\Lambda_0}$ if and only if for all $\gamma\in \operatorname{Aut}(\Lambda_0,F)\setminus \Gamma_{\operatorname{gen}}$ there exists a Dieudonné lattice $M\in \mathcal C_{\Lambda_0}(\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p)$ such that $\gamma\notin \operatorname{Aut}(M,F)$.

