[Lemma l:negligible.BCDE of arXiv:2601.12677, 'Stable and Fréchet limit theorem for subgraph functionals in the hyperbolic random geometr'] In the setting of Proposition (p:exp.clique of the paper), there exist $C, c_0 \in (0,\infty)$, both of which are independent of $n$ and $u$, such that 
\begin{equation*}
B_n(u) + \sum_{\ell=2}^{m-2} C_{n,\ell}(u) + D_n(u) + E_n(u) \le  \begin{cases}
C \beta_n e^{\frac{1}{2} (d-1)u}, & \text{for all } n \ge 1 \text{ and } u \in (0,{\gamma R_n}), \\[3pt]
Ce^{c_0\omega_n} \cdot e^{\frac{1}{2} (d-1)u}, & \text{for all } n \ge 1 \text{ and } u \in (0,R_n), 
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}
for some sequence $\beta_n\to0$.

