[Lemma lem:lipsde of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] \textbf{Continuity of solutions of SDEs} 
Let $g, \sigma$ be lipschitz continuous functions satisfying linear growth conditions. Denote by $\xi_t(x)$ the unique solution to 
\begin{align*}
d\xi_t =  g(\xi_s)ds +  \sigma(\xi_s)dB_s 
\end{align*}
with $\xi_0 = x$.  Suppose $h$ is a globally lipschitz continuous real vector valued function.  Then it holds that 
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E} \left[ |h(\xi_{s}(x)) - h(\xi_r(x))|^q  \right] \leq C(x)|s-r|^{q/2}
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

