[Lem lem-cut-equiv of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] For $n\in \mathbbm N_0$, let $\widehat\lambda^-_n$ be the initial vertex of $\widehat\lambda_n$. The following are equivalent. 
\begin{itemize}
\item $\widehat\lambda^-_n$ is a cut vertex for $\widehat M$ and $\widehat\lambda^-_j \not= \widehat\lambda^-_n$ for each $j\leq n-1$. 
\item The event $A_n\cap B_n$ occurs, where 
\begin{equation}  
A_n := \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ \widehat{\mathcal R}(n) \leq \widehat{\mathcal R}(j) -1 ,\: \forall j \leq  n-1 \aftergroup\egroup\originalright\} \quad \text{and} \quad 
B_n := \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ \widehat{\mathcal L}(j) \geq \widehat{\mathcal L}(n)   ,\: \forall j \geq n   \aftergroup\egroup\originalright\} .
\end{equation}  
\end{itemize}

