body:
[Lemma lem:free-energy-spiked of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Fix $\theta>1$ and let $ \alpha >0$. The free energy of the spiked matrix model is given by:
\begin{align} 
F(\alpha,\theta) := \lim_{N \to \infty}  \frac{1}{N} \log \int_{\mathbf{S}_N} e^{\beta H_N(x)} dx = 
\begin{cases}
    \frac{\alpha^2}{4\theta^2} &\text{if} \ \alpha <1 \\
 \frac{\alpha}{2\theta} (\theta + \frac{1}{\theta}) - \frac{1}{4\theta^2} - \frac{1}{2} \log(\alpha) - \frac{1}{2}         &\text{else} 
\end{cases} \, ,
\end{align}
where the limit exists $\mathbb{P}_M$ almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

