[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2607.29327, 'Fractal Random Variables\\ Defined by Probability Distributions of Digits\\ of Their $G_2$'] Hausdorff--Besicovitch dimension of the set
  $B[G_2; p_0]=\{x: \nu_0(x)=p_0\}$
  is calculated by formula
  \begin{equation}

    \alpha_0(E)=\frac{\ln{p_0^{p_0}p_1^{p_1}}}{\ln g_0^{p_0}(-g_1)^{p_1}}.
  \end{equation}

[Defi defi of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] A functional $\Phi: \mathbb{D}^d \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is called $L^{\infty}\text{-Lipschitz}$, if there exists a constant $\Lambda_{\Phi}> 0$ such that 
				\begin{align}
					|\Phi(\bold{x}_1)-\Phi(\bold{x}_2)| \leq \Lambda_{\Phi} \sup_{ 0\leq t\leq T}|\bold{x}_1(t) -\bold{x}_2(t)|, \quad  \forall \bold{x}_1,\bold{x}_2 \in \mathbb{D}^d; 
				\end{align}
				and $\Phi: \mathbb{D}^d \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is called $L^{1}\text{-Lipschitz}$, if it satisfies
				\begin{align}
					|\Phi(\bold{x}_1)-\Phi(\bold{x}_2)| \leq \Lambda_{\Phi} \int_{ 0}^{T}|\bold{x}_1(t) -\bold{x}_2(t)|\mathrm{d}t, \quad  \forall \bold{x}_1,\bold{x}_2 \in \mathbb{D}^d.
				\end{align}

