Note that the probability law of $s_{d-1} \left( \mathcal{C}(\tau) \right)$ is equal to that of the total progeny of a branching process with offspring distribution $d \mathsf{Poi}(\lambda)$. $\mathcal{C}$ denote the total progeny ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:a63a8360d286fdd59cba4bc0766a10b106d5fce4b543cc9ba29a0f5cbaf6b5f3","revision_digest":"sha256:cd7d67c893a8557ad5ad9be752839c462595f50f504ab3a41173d7ba5030ea1d","source_id":"arxiv:2605.03151","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

