[Lemma 28 (Spectral concentration of the rescaled fluctuation matrix) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Suppose Assumption \ref{assump:random_matrix} holds, and let $s_{\max}$ be the maximum variance defined in \eqref{eq:def_s_star}, $\A$ and $\check{\A}$ be the rescaled and comparison fluctuation matrices defined in \eqref{eq:def_check_A_and_A}. Let $t_D$, $\tau$, and $\eps_{\textup{pot}}$ be as in Theorem \ref{thm:first_approximation_rescaled}, and assume $\eps_{\textup{pot}} \le 1$. Then, on the event $\mathcal{E}_{2} \cap \{\|\X-\bLambda\|_2 \le t_D\}$,
	\begin{align}

		&\|\A\A^T - \check{\A}\check{\A}^T\|_2 \le \eps_{\textup{cov}} := \frac{3\, e^{4K}\, N^2}{(m+n)\,s_{\textup{max}}\,\|\bLambda\|_1^2}\, \eps_{\textup{pot}}\, t_D^2\, (2 + 3\eps_{\textup{pot}}).
	\end{align}

