[Lem trace power mixed products including bfE of arXiv:2608.23156, 'Disc counting statistics of the real Ginibre ensemble'] Under the assumptions of
Lemma~(lem: trace power bfL-n-R asymp of the paper), let $p$ be a fixed
positive integer, and let $a_\nu,b_\nu,c_\nu,d_\nu$ be fixed
nonnegative integers for $\nu=1,\ldots,p$. Suppose that
\begin{equation}
    \sum_{\nu=1}^p(a_\nu+b_\nu)\geq1.
\end{equation}
Then, as $N=2n\to\infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{Tr}\bigg[
        \prod_{\nu=1}^p
        \mathbf{E}_{N,1}(R)^{a_\nu}
        \mathbf{E}_{N,2}(R)^{b_\nu}
        \mathbf{M}_N(R)^{c_\nu}
        \mathbf{L}_N(R)^{d_\nu}
    \bigg]
    =
    o(\sqrt n).
\end{equation}

