[Proposition second_moment_bounded_degree of arXiv:2606.27357, '\textbf{Typical distances in high-genus triangulations}'] Let $n, g \ge 1$ such that $n \ge 2g-1$ and let $\mathbf{p} = (p_1,\cdots,p_{\ell}) \in (\mathbb{N}^{*})^{\ell}$. Denoting by $e_1$ the root edge on $\partial_1 T_{n,g,\mathbf{p}}$ and by $\rho_1$ its starting point, we have 
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}[\deg_{T_{n,g,\mathbf{p}}}(\rho_1)^2] \le 4 + 5 \frac{\tau_{\mathbf{p}}(n+1,g)}{\tau_{\mathbf{p}}(n,g)}+ 16\frac{\tau_{\mathbf{p}}(n+2,g)}{\tau_{\mathbf{p}}(n,g)}.
\end{align*}

Moreover, for any $\theta \in [0,\frac{1}{2})$, there exists $C_{\theta} > 0$ such that  for any $\frac{g_n}{n} \to \theta \in [0,\frac{1}{2})$ and $\mathbf{p}^n = (p_1^n,\cdots,p_{\ell_n}^n) \in (\mathbb{N}^{*})^{\ell_n}$ such that $|\mathbf{p}^n| = o(n)$, for $n$ large enough
\begin{align*}
\forall x \in \partial T_{n,g_n,\mathbf{p}^n}, \qquad \mathbb{E}[(D_x^n)^2] \le C_{\theta}.
\end{align*}
Therefore by (equation bound of the paper), for $n$ large enough,
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\big[|\partial^{*}B^{\bullet}(n)|^2\big]
\le \mathbb{E}\big[|B^{+}(n)|^2\big]
\le 4C_{\theta}|\mathbf{p}^{n}|^2.
\end{align*}

