[Propo pro:aprioriestim of arXiv:2412.01673, 'Spatial SIR epidemic model with varying infectivity without movement of individuals'] Let $T>0$, and let $(\overline{\mu}^S,\overline{\mu}^{\mathfrak{F}} )$  be a solution of the first two equations of (equation syst of the paper). Then there exists  positive constants $C$ 	
	and $c$ such that:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item $\forall t\in[0;T],$ $\|\overline{\mu}^{S}(t,.)\|_{\infty}\leq C;$
		\item $\displaystyle \inf_{y\in D} \int_{D}K(z,y)\overline{\mu}(z)dz \ge c$;
		\item $\forall t\in[0;T]$; $\|\overline{\mu}^{\mathfrak{F}}(t,.)\|_{\infty}\leq C.$
	\end{itemize}

