[Prop 7 of arXiv:2609.01231, 'MULTI-HEAD SELF ATTENTION IS A PARAMETER IDENTIFICATION MECHANISM'] Using a RoPE encoding in a transformer we have $D$-dimensional invariance in query-key products ($(\C \setminus \{0\})^{D/2}$ instead of $GL_D(\R)$) of the form 
\begin{equation*}
	\vec{S} = \begin{pmatrix}
		\alpha_1 e^{i\theta_1} & \vec{0} & \dotsb & \vec{0} \\
		\vec{0} & \alpha_2 e^{i\theta_2} & \dotsb & \vec{0} \\
		\vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\
		\vec{0} & \vec{0} & \dotsb & \alpha_{D/2} e^{i\theta_{D/2}} \\
	\end{pmatrix}
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Satz thm:target-statement-necessity of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d\in\mathds{N}$, $s,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\theta \in\mathds{R}$, and $p,q\in (0,\infty]$.
Assume that $a$ follows a Besov sequence prior with parameters $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\theta)$ and template random variable $X$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
\mathds{P}(X\neq 0)>0.
\end{equation}
If $a\in b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)$ almost surely, then also Property A is satisfied.

