[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2606.31936, 'Coupling and Maximal Inequalities for Graph-Dependent Empirical Processes'] Suppose $\sup_{ f \in \mathcal F } ||f||_{\infty} < \infty$ and, for each $n$, there exists:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item A partition
		\(\mathcal P_n=\{B_1,\ldots,B_{M_n}\}\) of \(N_n\), with
		\(\max_m |B_m|\le q_n\), and an associated \(r_n\)-coloring,
		\item A  finite partition of \(\mathcal F\), \(T_{L_{n}}\)
	\end{itemize}
	such that for some $a,b$
	\begin{align}
		\left( \frac{
			\sqrt{ K_{r_{n}}}	}{\sqrt n}  \max_{m\in[M_n]}\Gamma_p(B_m)    \right)   2^{\frac{\lceil a L_{n} \rceil}{2}}  \to 0 ~and~	\left(  \frac{K_{r_{n}}  q_n}{n}
		+	\bar{\tau}_{\operatorname{cone} \Pi[T_{L_{n}}]  ,G_n}
		\left( 	\mathcal P_{n}, 	\mathcal C_{r_{n}}[\mathcal P_{n} ] \right)    \right)   2^{\lceil b L_{n} \rceil}   \to 0, 	
	\end{align}
	and
	\begin{align}
		\frac{1}{n}
		\sum_{i\in N_n}
		\mathbb E 	\left[  \sup_{C\in T_{L_n}} D_C(Z_i) \right] \to 0,

	\end{align}
	as $n \to \infty$. Then \(  (\mathcal F,G_{n}) \) is graph Glivenko--Cantelli, i.e.,
	\begin{align}
		\sup_{f\in\mathcal F}
		\left| \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i \in N_{n}} \{ f(Z_{i}) - \mathbb E[f(Z_{i})]   \}  \right|
		=
		o_{\mathbb P}(1).
	\end{align}

[Theorem Delay blow up-NS of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Let $\frac{1}{4}\leq a<\frac{1}{2}<2b+a$ and $\nu>0$. Fix $R_0>0$ and $0<\epsilon<1$, then there exists $N_0=N_0(\nu,R_0,\epsilon)$, such that for all $N>N_0$ and initial data $u_0$ satisfying 
		\begin{equation*}
			u_0\in H^{2b+a} \quad \text{and}\quad \|u_0\|_{H^{2b+a}}\leq R_0, 
		\end{equation*}
		the equation (equation NS-u_n of the paper) admits a unique strong solution which is spatially smooth and, with a probability no less than $1-\epsilon$, exists globally on $[0,\infty)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

