[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2606.06757, 'Path-Dependent Ergodic Optimal Control \\ and Backward Stochastic Differential Equations'] Let $(a_n)_{n\ge1}$ be a sequence in $\mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\sup_{m,n\ge 1}
|a_{n+m}-a_n-a_m|<\infty$.
Then there exists $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$ such that $\sup_{n\ge1}|a_n-\lambda n|<\infty$. In particular, $\frac{a_n}{n}\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\lambda$.

