body:
[Lemma 54 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the notation in Lemma \ref{Lem.PowerSeriesSG}. There exist constants $\delta_2 \in (0,\delta_0]$ and $\epsilon_2 > 0$, depending on $q, \kappa, c$, such that for $r \in [0, \delta_2]$
\begin{equation}
\Real \left [\GFt(z) - \GFt(c) \right] \geq \epsilon_2 \cdot r^2, \mbox{ if } z = c + r e^{\pm \im \pi/2}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma det-martingale-limit of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] For every $\varphi\in C^\infty(\mathbb{T}^d)$, write 
		\begin{equation*}
			M_t^N(\varphi) = \sum_k \int_{0}^{t}\big\< \sigma_k^N\cdot\nabla (-\Delta)^{a} \omega^N,\varphi\big\> \, {\,\rm d} W^k,\quad \forall t\geq0.
		\end{equation*}
		Then for every $T>0$, $\big|\sup\limits_{t\in [0,T]}M_t^N(\varphi)\big|\rightarrow 0$ in probability as $N\rightarrow \infty$.

