[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Let~$\hat\epsilon, \eta, a$ be as in Lemma~\ref{l:lyapunov}.  Then, for all~$\epsilon \le \hat\epsilon$ and all~$h$ satisfying~$0<h/\epsilon^2 \le \eta$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \gap(\hat P_{h, \epsilon}\vert_{B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})}) \geq 2^{-4} \gap(\bar P_{h, \epsilon}\vert_{B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})})\,.
    \end{equation}
    Here, $\bar P_{h, \epsilon}\vert_{B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})}$ denotes the restriction of the chain $\bar P_{h,\epsilon}$ to $B(m_1, a\sqrt{\epsilon})$, where $\bar P_{h,\epsilon}$ is Metropolis random walk with step size~$h$ and the normal stationary distribution~$N(m_1, \epsilon D^2 U(m_1)^{-1})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

