[Lemma lem:gap-multikink of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] Let $Q \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $Q\ge 2$.
For $d>0$ sufficiently large, there exists $c>0$ such that
for all $\xi_1,\dots,\xi_Q \in \mathbb{R} $ with  $\min_{i \neq j} |\xi_i-\xi_j|=d $, 
one has 
\begin{align*}
E(m_{\xi_1,\dots,\xi_Q} ) \ge |Q| E_{\textup{kink}}+c\cdot e^{- d}.
\end{align*}

