[Lemma lem:gaussian-soft-head of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Fix $J$ with $|J|\le K_d$ and condition on
$W_J=w\in\mathfrak{G}_J$.  Uniformly in the realized good head,
\begin{equation}
\min_{y \in \mathcal{Y}_J} \max_{S \in \mathcal{S}_J} \sum_{i \notin J} y_i
\ip{G_i}{S} \;\ge\; c_0\,d
\end{equation}
except with conditional probability at most
$e^{-c_{\mathrm{prob}}d^2}$.  Moreover, for all sufficiently large $d$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}_G\Phi_J(G;w)\ge c_1d.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:Delta-moments of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] For the $\Delta$ in Equation~(equation eq:Delta-def of the paper),
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{E}[\Delta^2]&\le C_H\gamma^2s_{\gamma,N},                              \\
  \mathbb{E}[\Delta^4]&\le C_H\gamma^7,                                         \\
  \mathbb{E}|\Delta|^6&\le C_H\gamma^9.                                         
\end{align}
A second, weaker but sometimes useful estimate is
\begin{equation}

  \mathbb{E}[\Delta^4]\le C_H\gamma^4(M_4+\gamma^4),
  \qquad M_4:=\mathbb{E}[x^4].
\end{equation}

[Lemma rank_r_expectation_lemma of arXiv:2411.04795, 'Metastable Distributions of Semi-Markov Processes'] Let $1 \le  r < R$  and $ 1 \le i \le M.$ For $1\le s \le r$, let $j_s$ be such that $\pi^{s}(S_i) = S^s_{j_s}$, Then
 $$\lim \limits_{\varepsilon \to 0} \ \mathbb E \left({N^{\varepsilon}(x, i, r)}\right) \times  \prod_{s = 0}^{r-1} \left( ({\lambda^{s}(j_s)})^{-1}
 \displaystyle  \sum_{\substack{j \ : \ S_j^s \subseteq \pi^{s+1}(S_i) \\ k \ : \ S_k^s \not \subseteq \pi^{s+1}(S_i)} }  {\lambda^{s}(j)}P_{jk}^{s, \varepsilon} \right) = 1$$  uniformly in $x \in \pi^{r}(S_i). $ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

