body:
[Theorem 35 (Conformal martingales transforms; real-valued) of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Let $M_t=\int_0^t K_s\cdot dB_s$ be  a martingale on the filtration of $d$-dimensional Brownian motion as in \eqref{StochasticMartin}.   
 Let $(A,B)$ be a conformal $d\times d$ pair and suppose in addition that $\|A\|=\|B\|\leq 1$. 
Define $X_t:=A*M_t$ and $Y_t:=B*M_t.$ Set 
\begin{align*}
Z_t:=X_t+iY_t=(A+iB)*M_t. 
\end{align*}
Then $Z_t$ is a conformal martingale and 
\begin{align}
\|A+iB\|_{L^p(\Omega)}\leq 
\frac{1}{C_p(2)}(p^*-1), \quad 1<p<\infty,  
\end{align}
where $C_p(2)$ is as in Remark \ref{Asym:C_p}.

