[Lemma lm:standard_arg of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] For every $\vartheta > 0$, there exists $\beta_* > 0$ such that the following holds: Assume that there are $\tilde \sigma \in (\tfrac{3}{4}, 1)$ and $\theta > 0$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{n \to \infty} n^{\theta} \sup_{\|y\| \leq n^{\tilde \sigma}} D^{\vartheta}_n(y) = 0.  
\end{equation*}
Then, if $\beta \leq \beta_*$, one has 
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{t \to \infty} t^{\theta /2} \sup_{\|y\| \leq t^{\sigma}} \frac{1}{p_t^y} \mathbf{E} \left[q_{n_{t}}^y \left \langle \left \lvert \mathcal{T}(y; 0,t) \right \rvert \right \rangle \right] = 0
\end{equation*}
for every $\sigma \in (0, \tilde \sigma)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

