[Theorem thm:xi of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] Let $E$ be an edge-measured graph corresponding to a graph $G$ and a measure $\psi$, as described above. Let $G^{1/2}$ be the set of vertices and midpoints of the edges of  $G$. If:
		\begin{itemize}
			\item the same assumptions of (thm:criterion-edge of the paper) hold,
			\item $\alpha_0$ is a multiple of $\alpha_1$ and they are both supported on the diagonal of $(\partial G)^2$, and \item the function $t\mapsto \nu(\mathrm{Lip}_1^{\leq t})$ has a continuous derivative,
		\end{itemize}
		then the distribution of $\left((\Theta_i)_{i\geq 1}, \restrict{\mathrm{Vor}(\Phi)}{G^{1/2}} \right)$ does not depend on $\xi$. In addition, $\restrict{\mathrm{Vor}(X^{(\lambda)})}{G^{1/2}}$  converges weakly to $\restrict{\mathrm{Vor}(\Phi)}{G^{1/2}}$ as $\lambda\downarrow 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

