[Lemma lem:g>zda of arXiv:2509.17319, 'Non-directed polymers in random environments with range penalties: the high-dimensional ca'] Recall $\Omega_r(\Delta)$ from Section (S:notations of the paper). If $\gamma>\zeta+\frac{d-\alpha}{\alpha}$, $A_N\le N$, 
then for any $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$ and $p>1$, there exists a constant $C=C_{d,p,\varepsilon}>0$, such that
\begin{multline}
\sum_{k=0}^{\log_p(\frac{N}{A_N})}\sum_{j=0}^{B_{N,k}}{\ensuremath{\mathbbm P}} \Bigg(\max\limits_{S\in {\ensuremath{\mathcal A}} _{j,k} }\Omega_{p^{k+1}A_N}({\ensuremath{\mathcal R}} _N(S))>\varepsilon^2p^{k+j}\frac{h_N}{\beta_N}A_N\Bigg)
\le C(\log N) (N^{-\zeta+\gamma-\frac{d-\alpha}\alpha})^{-\frac{\alpha d}{\alpha+d}},
\end{multline}
where
\begin{equation}
B_{N,k}:=\log_p\Big(\frac{|\Lambda_{p^k A_N}|}{A_N}\wedge \frac{N}{p^k A_N}\Big)
\end{equation}
and ${\ensuremath{\mathcal A}} _{j,k}={\ensuremath{\mathcal A}} _{j,k}(p,N) := {\ensuremath{\mathcal M}} _p(p^kA_N, p^j)$ (see (equation eq:Mrs of the paper)), that is,
\begin{equation}
{\ensuremath{\mathcal A}} _{j,k} =\Big\{S\colon \,  M_N(S)\in [p^kA_N, p^{k+1}A_N],\, |{\ensuremath{\mathcal R}} _N(S)|\in [p^{k}p^{j}A_N ,p^{k+1}p^{j+1}A_N]\Big\}.
\end{equation}

