[Proposition lyons1989 of arXiv:2604.24389, '``True" self-avoiding walks on general trees'] Let $\mathbf{Q}$ be a quasi-independent percolation process taking place on an infinite locally finite tree $\mathcal T = (V,E)$.
    \begin{itemize}
        \item [(i)] If \(\inf_{\pi \in \Pi} \sum_{e \in \pi} \mathbf{Q}(\rho \leftrightarrow e^+) = 0 \text{ then } \mathbf{Q}(\rho \leftrightarrow \infty) = 0\);
