[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2607.22416, 'A multi-player optimal stopping game based on a spider Brownian bridge'] There exists a Nash equilibrium in the multi-player version of the optimal stopping game with linear payoffs, if for every $i\in\{1,...,N\}$ 
    \begin{equation}

        p_iQ_i^i+ \sum_{j\neq i,j=1}^N p_jQ_j^i\geq0.
    \end{equation}

