body:
[Theorem thm: moments of arXiv:2411.12474, 'Multi-type branching processes with immigration generated by point processes'] In the case of immigration spanned by a $(\Lambda, K)$-DPP,	\begin{enumerate}
		\item  we have that
		\[\Ebb{{Z}_i(t)} = \int_{(0,t]}
		K(x,x)\Ebb{Z_{\times,i}(t-x)}\Lambda(\mathrm{d} x),\]
		\item and if we assume (equation eq:strong of the paper),
        \begin{align*}
			Cov(Z_i(t), Z_j(t))=&
			\int_{(0,t]} K(x,x)
		 \Ebb{Z_{\times, i}(t-x) Z_{\times, j}(t-x)} \Lambda(\mathrm{d} x) \\
& \! - \int_{(0,t]^2} K^2(x,y) \Ebb{Z_{\times, i}(t-x)} \Ebb{Z_{\times, j}(t-y)} \Lambda(\mathrm{d} x) \Lambda(\mathrm{d} y).
		\end{align*}
	\end{enumerate}

