[Definition def:cigar-shape of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $A, B$ with angle denoted $\theta_{A, B}$ and $B_1 - A_1 = M_{A, B}$. Define the curves $\ensuremath{\mathcal C}^\pm_{A, B}$ by
		\begin{equation*}
			\ensuremath{\mathcal C}^\pm(t) = \tan(\theta_{A, B})(t-A_1) + \left(\frac{(t - A_1)(M_{A, B} - t + A_1)}{M_{A, B}}\right)^{1/2}(\log L)^2\,.
		\end{equation*}
		Define the cigar shape ${\ensuremath{\mathscr C}} = {\ensuremath{\mathscr C}}(\overline{AB})$ as the region in between the curves $\ensuremath{\mathcal C}^+_{A, B}$ and $\ensuremath{\mathcal C}^-_{A, B}$.

