This follows by combining \pref{lem:alg-resolvent-lipschitz-DQ} with the Lipschitzness of $\tanh$ and the multiplicativity of Lipschitz constants under composition of functions.

  \par\Needspace{\ppartneed}\addvspace{\smallskipamount}
  \noindent\textit{Lipschitzness of $\widehat f^*$.}\hspace{0.5em}\ignorespaces

Since $\tanh$ is Lipschitz, it suffices to bound the Lipschitz constant of $\widehat f^*(x)$ as a function of $m := \tanh(x)$.
By product rule, this Lipschitz constant is bounded by
\[ \norm{m \mapsto E_{\mathcal{D}_n}\left( {\widehat Q(m)^2} ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:ae2a701b7e8da6ad8fe1294b69101bdd434451f7f2a62e3a1e40079c16bbbdc1","revision_digest":"sha256:d5acbe1868c49dd23d9114639507baa3d681a0db252c73ebedbd16c11b30c5b9","source_id":"arxiv:2605.03718","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

