[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2609.01237, ''] Define the bilinear form  $(\,\cdot\, , \,\cdot\,)_{\cH}$  via  
	\begin{align*}
(v,w)_{\cH} \coloneqq \left(v^{(1)},w^{(1)}\right)_{H^1(\Omega_1)}, \quad  \forall \, v,w \in \cH,
	\end{align*}
where $v^{(1)} \coloneqq \restr{v}{\Omega_1}$ and $w^{(1)} \coloneqq \restr{w}{\Omega_1}$. Then $\left(\cH, (\,\cdot\, , \,\cdot\,)_{\cH} \right)$ is a Hilbert space. The associated norm is defined as usual, by $\|v\|_{\cH} \coloneqq \sqrt{(v,v)_{\cH}}$, for all $v\in\mathcal{H}$.

