[Lemma lem:unit-jitter of arXiv:2609.00399, 'Shannon's problem on the monotonicity of entropy and a Conjecture of Tao'] Let $Y$ be a finitely supported $G$-valued random variable and let
$\xi\sim\operatorname{Unif}[0,1)$ be independent.  Relative to
(equation eq:quotient-Haar-cells of the paper),
\begin{equation}
 h(j(Y)+e(\xi))=H(Y).
\end{equation}
Let $A,B$ be independent random variables in the same locally compact abelian group.  If $A$
has a Haar density, then
\begin{equation}
 h(A+B)\geq h(A)
\end{equation}
whenever both entropies are finite real numbers.

