[Corollary cor:srd-L^2 of arXiv:2506.17168, '{\bf Scaling limits for sample autocovariance operators of Hilbert space-valued linear pro'] Let $\{X_n\}_{n \in \mathbb Z}$ be an $L^2(\mathbb{Y})$-valued process (equation eq:XninL2 of the paper) and consider its autocovariance operators $( \widehat \gamma_{N,h}, h = 0,\dots,H)$ given in (equation eq:gammars of the paper), where we consider $\widehat \gamma_{N,h}$ as an element of $\operatorname{HS}(L^2(\mathbb{Y}))$ for all $h$, with a slight abuse of notation. Suppose $\operatornamewithlimits{ess\text{ }sup}_{s \in \mathbb Y} d(s) < \frac{1}{4}$ and
\begin{equation} 
  \operatorname{E} \| \varepsilon_{0} \|^4_{L^2(\mathbb{Y})} < \infty. 
\end{equation}
Then, 
    \begin{equation}
        \sqrt{N} \begin{pmatrix}
            \widehat \gamma_{N,0} - \gamma_{0} \\
            \vdots \\
            \widehat \gamma_{N,H} - \gamma_{H}
        \end{pmatrix} \xrightarrow{d} 
        G \doteq
        \begin{pmatrix}
            G_0 \\
            \vdots \\
            G_H
        \end{pmatrix} \in \left(\operatorname{HS}(L^2(\mathbb{Y})\right)^{\times (H+1)},
    \end{equation}
    where the convergence holds in the topology of $(\operatorname{HS}(L^2(\mathbb{Y})))^{\times (H+1)}$, $G$ is a centered Gaussian element,
     and the covariance operator of $G$ is the operator $\Sigma$ given in (equation eq:Sigma of the paper)--(equation def:def:Aq-C of the paper), for $p,q=0,\dots, H$, and with $\mathbb{H}$ replaced by $L^2(\mathbb Y)$.

