[Theorem prop:alpha_llt of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $p_n(x,y)$ denote the $n$-step transition probability associated with the transition matrix $P_N$ from Definition~(defmodel of the paper), with profile $f_\alpha(x)$, where $N=L^d$.
  If $ne^{-c_{\alpha}W^\alpha}=o(1)$ as $N\to \infty$, then
    \begin{equation}
