[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2608.20252, '2608.20252'] A family $Q^N$ of probability measures on $\mathcal{D}([0,T], \Omega)$ is tight exactly when
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] For each $t\in [0,T]$, the distributions of $\pi_t$ under $Q^N$ are tight.
\item[(2)] For every $\epsilon>0$, $\lim_{\gamma\downarrow 0}\lim_{N\uparrow\infty} Q^N(\pi: w'_\pi(\gamma)>\epsilon) = 0$.
\end{itemize}
Moreover, a sufficient condition for $(2)$ is
\begin{itemize}
\item[(2')] In condition $(2)$, replace $w'_\pi$ with $w_\pi$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

