[Lemma hitting_probability_upper_bound_on_Z of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] For every $\ell > 0$, there exists $C = C(d, \alpha, K, \ell) > 0$ such that
\begin{align}
    \frac{C^{-1}}{|x - y|^{\alpha + d}} \le \mathbf P_x(\tau_y \le \ell) \le \frac{C}{|x - y|^{\alpha + d}},
\end{align}
for any $x, y \in \mathbb Z^d$ with $x \neq y$.

