[Proposition lem:kurtz of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] The operator \fs{${\mathscr G}_{\hat\alpha,k}\coloneqq\Pi_k A_{\hat\alpha,k}|_{\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k)}:\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k)\to\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k)$} is an infinitesimal generator  on $\ensuremath{\mathcal R}(\Pi_k) \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{\Xi_k}$. Moreover,  we have the following  convergence:
\begin{equation}
\lim_{\varepsilon\to 0} \max_{\eta \in \Xi_k}\left|e^{t\tttonde{A_{\hat \alpha,k}+\varepsilon^{-1}B_k}}  f(\eta) - e^{t\fs{{\mathscr G}_{\hat\alpha,k}}} \Pi_k f(\eta) \right| = 0 \; \text{,}\;\;\qquad t>0\; \text{,}\;\; f \in \mathbb{R}^{\Xi_k} \; \text{.}
\end{equation}

