[Lemma lem:Feynman of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] Fix $t>0$ and $x\in{\mathbb{R}}^3\backslash \{0\}$. Then, \begin{align*}
u^\varepsilon(t,x)\to S_tu_0(x)+\sqrt{\pi}\int_{0}^{\infty}e^{\gamma v}\text{\rm d} v \int_{0<u<s<t}\text{\rm d} up_u(x)\mathbb{P}(\zeta_v\in \text{\rm d} s)S_{t-s}u_0(0)
\end{align*}
for $u_0\in C_b\left({\mathbb{R}}^3\right)$, where $S_tu_0(x)=\int_{{\mathbb{R}}^3}p_t(x,y)u_0(y)\text{\rm d} y$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

