[Definition 82 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] For disjoint sets $A, B \subset V$, we define the effective resistance between $A$ and $B$ by 
\begin{equation} 
    \effR{G, \weight}{A}{B} := \frac{1}{\sum_{a \in A} \weight(a) Q_{a}(\tau_B < \tau_A^+)}, 
\end{equation}
where $Q_a$ is the law of the lazy random walk started at $a$, $\tau_B$ is the first hitting time of $B$, and $\tau_A^+$ is the first return time to $A$. When $A=\{a\}$ and $B = \{b\}$ are singletons, we will just write
$\effR{G, \weight}{a}{b}$ instead. When the underlying graphs and weights are clear we will often drop either one or both of the superscripts.

[Thm T th gau of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exist a deterministic constant $c_1\in(0,\infty)$
  and a deterministic function $c_2\colon (0,\infty)\to(0,\infty)$ such that,
  $\hat{P}_{\bm{\rho}}$-a.s., for all $t \in (0,\infty)$,
  \begin{equation}
    c_1
    \leq
    \sup_{s\in[0,t]}
    \varlimsup_{\delta\downarrow0}
    \frac{\mathcal{C}_t([s-\delta,s+\delta])}
    {\delta^{d_{\mathrm{ct}}}(\log(1/\delta))^{\hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}}^*/2}}
    \leq
    \varlimsup_{\delta\downarrow0}
    \sup_{s\in[0,t]}
    \frac{\mathcal{C}_t([s-\delta,s+\delta])}
    {\delta^{d_{\mathrm{ct}}}(\log(1/\delta))^{\hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}}^*/2}}
    \leq
    c_2(t).
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:basisconvolution of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] There exist polynomials $P_{k,j,\ell}$ each of degree $k$ such that 
\begin{align}
&\sum_{k=2}^{n-1}
        \frac{z^m}{k^{j+1/2}(n-k)^{\ell+1/2}}
        e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 (n-k)}}
=
    {\rm sgn}(z)\sqrt{2\pi}
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2n}}
    \frac{Q_{j,\ell,m}(z/\sqrt{n})}{n^{\ell+j-m/2}}
        \\
\nonumber   
&\hspace{1cm}+
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2n}}
    \frac{z^m}{n^{\ell+1/2}}
    \sum_{k=0}^{\lceil \frac{r+m}{2}\rceil - \ell+1}
        \frac{P_{k,j,\ell}(z^2/n)}{n^{k}}
+
    O\left(\frac{1}{(\min(\sqrt{n},1+|z|))^{r+3}}\right),
\end{align}
where
\begin{align*}
    Q_{j,\ell,m}(t)
=
    t^m
    \sum_{q=0}^{j}
        \gamma_{q,j,\ell} t^{2q}
        \sum_{k=0}^{\ell+j+q-1}
            \frac{(2k-1)!!
            \binom{\ell+j+q-1}{k}}
            {t^{2k+1}}
\end{align*}
and the reals $\gamma_{q,j,\ell}$ can be computed recursively; the corresponding expressions are given in (equation eq:gammas of the paper) below. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 76 (Split Rees realization) of arXiv:2608.08756, 'Infinite-Dimensional L\'evy Area and Spectral Ancestry'] Let \((H,\omega,{\mathbf X}^{(2)})\) be a controlled critical normal
entrance, and let \(L_n(s,t)\) be the homogeneous logarithms of its geometric
extension.  Its split Rees logarithm through degree \(N\) is
\begin{equation}
 \mathbf C_{\le N}({\mathbf X})_{s,t}
 :=X_{s,t}+\sum_{n=2}^N\sum_{r=1}^{\lfloor n/2\rfloor}
 z^{-r}P_{n,r}L_n(s,t).

\end{equation}
Changing the splitting changes the displayed lift, but not the first nonzero
normal coefficient modulo the next filtration level.

[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2605.10452, 'A secretary for Messrs. Luce and Mallows'] \begin{equation*}
\min(V_1,V_2,\cdots, V_r)\sim\text{\rm Exp}(\sum_{i=1}^r\theta_i),\ r\in\mathbb{N}.
\end{equation*}
\begin{proof}
$$
P(\min(V_1,V_2,\cdots, V_r)\ge x)=\prod_{i=1}^rP(V_i\ge x)=\prod_{i=1}^r e^{-\theta_ix}=e^{-(\sum_{i=1}^r\theta_i)x}.
$$
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def:bulk dist limit of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] Let $\xi_{\Gamma}$ be the measure introduced in Proposition~(prop:feasibility of the paper). We call $\xi_{\Gamma}$ the generating measure with perturbation $\Gamma$, and define
    \begin{equation}
