[Prop 16 of arXiv:2506.21087, 'Quasi-Stationary Distributions of Interacting Dynamical Systems and their approximation'] Assume \ref{condhzero} and \ref{condhun} and that there exist $\varepsilon>0$, $c>0$ and a probability distribution $\Psi$ such that for all $n$ and $\alpha$, $\KK^{\alpha}_{n+1,n}\geq\varepsilon\Psi$, $\|\KK^{\alpha}_{n+1,n}\|_{\infty}\leq c$ and 
    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{n}\frac{\Psi(g^{\alpha}_{n})}{\|g^{\alpha}_{n}\|_{\infty}}=+\infty.
    \end{equation}

    Then, Condition \eqref{eq:conditioncontractralphaaa} holds true.

