[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2604.05138, 'Convergence rate of $H$-property for step-graphons'] The following two items hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $W$ satisfies Condition $A$ and $B'$, but not $B$, then there exist a nonzero $p^*\in (0,1)$ and a positive constant $c$ such that
\begin{equation}
|P_n(W) - p^*| \leq \frac{c}{\sqrt{n}}.  
\end{equation}
\item If $W$ satisfies Condition $B'$, but not $A$, then there exist a positive constant $c$ such that 
\begin{equation}
P_n(W) \leq \frac{c}{\sqrt{n}}.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

