[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2608.13631, 'The classical discrete laws near the mode:\\ complete local expansions for the negative bi'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:hyp-main}, with $k=\mu+t$,
	\begin{equation}
		\log\Bigl[\sqrt{2\pi\,\frac{k\,(K-k)\,(n-k)\,(L+k)\,N}{K(N-K)\,n\,(N-n)}}\;P(k)\Bigr]
		\sim\sum_{m\ge1}\frac{\widehat A_m(t)}{N^{m}},
	\end{equation}
	with
	\begin{equation}
	\begin{gathered}
		\widehat A_m=\frac{(-1)^{m+1}}{m(m+1)}
		\Bigl[(W_m-1)\,B_{m+1}-\widehat\Xi_m\,\Bh_{m+1}(t)\Bigr],\\
		\widehat\Xi_m=(a^{-m}+d^{-m})
			+(-1)^{m+1}(b^{-m}+c^{-m}).
	\end{gathered}
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:D-Xt of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] Under Assumptions (ass:LR of the paper), (ass:diff2 of the paper), and~(ass:SC of the paper), the solution $X(t)$ belongs to $\mathbb{D}^{1,2}(H)$ for each $t \in [0, T]$, and its Malliavin derivative at time $r \in [0, t]$ is given by
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal{D}_r X(t) = Y(t,r)\,\mathcal{B}(r, X(r)),
\end{equation}
where $Y(t,r)$ is the first variation process (Definition (def:first-var of the paper)).

