[Theorem 72 (Evaluated reconstruction for $1\le r<2$) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $1\le r<2$, let the projections $P_\lambda,Q_\mu$ have finite rank,
and put
\begin{equation}

 d_{\lambda,\mu}:=\min\{\rank P_\lambda,\rank Q_\mu\}.
\end{equation}
Let
$K_{\lambda,\mu}\in
 \mathfrak W_{m,2}(\cH_{\R};Q_\mu\cC,P_\lambda\cE)$ and assume
\begin{equation}

 \sum_{\lambda,\mu}
 \left[
 d_{\lambda,\mu}^{1/r-1/2}
 \Prof_{m,2}(K_{\lambda,\mu})
 \right]^r<\infty.
\end{equation}
Then the block Wick series converges unconditionally in
$L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)$ for every $1\le p<\infty$.  With
$p_*:=\max\{p,r\}$,
\begin{align}

 &\norm{\sum_{\lambda,\mu}I_m(K_{\lambda,\mu})}
       _{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}\\
 &\quad\le
 A_m(p_*+2)^{m/2}
 \left\{
 \sum_{\lambda,\mu}
 \left[
 d_{\lambda,\mu}^{1/r-1/2}
 \Prof_{m,2}(K_{\lambda,\mu})
 \right]^r
 \right\}^{1/r}.
 \notag
\end{align}
The analogous decoupled assertion holds with $C_m$.  If the input and
output support families admit fixed orthogonality colorings with
$\chi_-$ and $\chi_+$ colors, respectively, the same assertions hold
with the right-hand sides multiplied by
$(\chi_+\chi_-)^{1-1/r}$.  A quantitative tail--defect form for moving
block families is given in
Proposition~\ref{prop:evaluated-tail-defect-below-Hilbert}.

