[Proposition prop:horizontal-torsion of arXiv:2609.00840, 'Kählerity of complete almost-Kähler gradient shrinking Ricci solitons'] Let $(M^{2m},g,J,\omega,f)$, $m\geq2$, be a complete almost-K\"ahler gradient shrinking Ricci soliton. Then, for $V=\nabla f$ and $W=JV$, we have
	\begin{equation*}
		(\nabla_X\omega)(Y,Z)=0
	\end{equation*}
	whenever any one of $X,Y,Z$ lies in
	$\operatorname{span}\{V,W\}$.

