\begin{equation}
\mathcal{M}'\coloneqq\min\{\sum_{v\in\mathcal{E}}\varphi_{v},\sum_{v\in\mathcal{E}}(1-\varphi_{v})\}.
\end{equation}
Note that $|\sigma_{\mathcal{E}}|=\sum_{v\in\mathcal{E}}\sigma_{v}\le\sum_{v\in\mathcal{E}}\varphi_{v}$
since by the hard-core restriction, for each $v\in\mathcal{E}$, $\sigma_{v}=1$
implies $\varphi_{v}=1$. Also, $|\sigma_{\mathcal{O}}|=\sum_{u\in\mathcal{O}}\sigma_{u}\le\sum_{v\in\mathcal{E}}(1-\varphi_{v})$
