[Proposition p:m2 of arXiv:2605.20587, 'Persistence and entropic repulsion of stationary Gaussian fields with spectral singularity'] Denote $m' =  \|\mu_{a.c.} + \mu_{s.c.}\|$. Then for every $\varepsilon > 0$ and $\beta \in [0,d)$, as $T \to \infty$, 
\[   -\log \inf_{\mu' \le \mu}  \mathbb{P} \Big[ \sup_{x \in B(T)} 
 |f_{\mu'}(x)| \le   \sqrt{2 (m' +\varepsilon) ( d - \beta)   \log T} \Big]  \le   T^{ ( \beta - \frac{\varepsilon}{2m'} (d-\beta))_+ + o(1)}  .\]

