[Lemma lm:L_convergence of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] For an inverse temperature $\beta \leq \beta_*$, the following is true: There is $\theta = \theta(\sigma) > 0$, independent of $\beta$, such that
\begin{equation} 
\lim_{t \to \infty} t^{\theta} \sup_{\|y\| \leq t^{\sigma}} \frac{1}{p_t^y} \biggl \langle \biggl \lvert \mathbf{E} \biggl[\mathbbm{1}_{q_{n_t}^y > 0} \ q_{n_t}^y \sum_{i=1}^3 L_i^{y,t}\biggr] \biggr \rvert \biggr \rangle  = 0. 
\end{equation}

[Cor precompactGraph of arXiv:2606.30517, '	extsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] In (prop:precompact2 of the paper), if  $E=G$ is a vertex-measured graph, $
u=\lim_n \lambda_n\iota^*_{t_n}\mu$ and  $ orall n: t_n\in\mathbb Z$
		then $(p_1-1)p_1^{j-1}\leq {
u(\mathrm{Lip}_1^j)}/{
u(\mathrm{Lip}_1^{\leq 0})}\leq (p_2-1)p_2^{j-1}$ for all $j\in\mathbb N$. In particular, if $p_1=p_2=p$, then $ orall j\in\mathbb Z:\ 
u(\mathrm{Lip}_1^j) = (p-1)p^{j-1+\xi}$ for some $\xi\in\mathbb R$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition of arXiv:2609.04072, 'Oort's conjecture for split unitary Shimura varieties'] For $s \geq 1$, we define the congruence subgroup of level $s$
    \begin{equation}
        V_s:=1+\pi^s\operatorname{Mat}_g(\mathcal{O}_D)\subset \operatorname{GL}_g(\mathcal{O}_D).
    \end{equation}
    Note that implicitly, $V_s$ depends on $g$, $m$ and $n$.

[Corollary 39 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Set~$A_1=(\beta_\ell,+\infty)$,~$A_2=(0,\beta_\ell)$,~$A_3=(-\frac{\alpha_1}{\gamma_1},0)$ and~$A_4=(-\infty,-\frac{\alpha_1}{\gamma_1})$. Let~$(\xi,\eta)\in (-1,1)^2$ be in the frozen component corresponding to~$A_{0,m}$ for some~$m=1,\dots,2(\ell+1)$, and let~$x$ and~$y$ be related to~$(\xi,\eta)$ by~\eqref{eq:global_coordinates_1xell}. If~$A_{0,m}\subset A_j$, for some~$j=1,\dots,4$, then
\begin{equation*}
\left(\cT(2(\ell x+i)+\eps,2(2 y+j')+\eps),\cO(2(\ell x+i)+\eps,2(2 y+j')+\eps)\right)\to P_j,
\end{equation*}
as~$N\to \infty$.

