body:
[Lemma 5 (Stable exit asymptotic and global bound) of arXiv:2608.17927, 'Near-unit-root persistence of symmetric stable \\ autoregressive sequences'] For every $0 < \alpha \leq 2$, there is a constant $c_{\alpha}\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for each $x > 0$,
\begin{equation}

\PP_{x}(\tau_{0}^{L} > T) \sim c_{\alpha} x^{\alpha/2}T^{-1/2}, \quad
T \to \infty.
\end{equation}
There is also a constant $C_{\alpha} < \infty$ such that, for all $x,T > 0$,
\begin{equation}

\PP_{x}(\tau_{0}^{L} > T) \leq C_{\alpha}\min\{1,\,x^{\alpha/2}T^{-1/2}\}.
\end{equation}

