[Lmm of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] In the setting of Theorem~(thrUniqLineSchw of the paper), we have that  $\lim_{T\to\infty}f(-T)=-\infty$ and $\lim_{T\to\infty}f(T)=\infty$ almost surely under both $\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathcal{P}$ and $\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathscr{M}_{\varkappa^2}^{\infty}$.
In other words,
\begin{align}
\mathcal{P}\left\{f: \, \lim_{T\to\infty}f(-T) = -\infty, \text{ and }   \lim_{T\to\infty}f(T) =\infty \right\} &=1;\\
\mathscr{M}_{\varkappa^2}^{\infty}\left\{f: \, \lim_{T\to\infty}f(-T) = -\infty, \text{ and }   \lim_{T\to\infty}f(T) =\infty\right\} &=1.
\end{align}

