[Defn def.relstab of arXiv:2504.19553, 'Extremal Ising Gibbs States on Lobachevsky lattices'] A configuration $\sigma^0 \in \Omega$ is $c$-stable if there exists a strictly positive constant $c>0$ such that the following inequality holds {\color{purple} [Matteo: Est-ce qu'on utilise cette definition après?]}
$$
H(\sigma)-H(\sigma^0)\geq c \cdot |V(\sigma \bigtriangleup \sigma^0)| \;
$$
for all $\sigma \in \Omega$ satisfying $V(\sigma \bigtriangleup \sigma^0) \Subset V$.

