[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2609.03793, 'Typical martingale diverges on a co-$\sigma$-porous set'] Let $p\in[1, \infty)$ and $k\geq1$ be arbitrary. Then
\begin{equation*}
\bs{\f\in\M_p;\s{\eta\in2^\N;\osc f_n(\eta)\geq k}\text{ is comeager in }(2^\N,\rhoharm)}
\end{equation*}
is co-$\sigma$-porous in $\M_p$.

