body:
[Corollary 41 (Contractivity of symmetrization for the decoupled profile) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Under the assumptions of Proposition~\ref{prop:wick-decoupling}, for every $2\le r\le\infty$,
\begin{equation}

  \Prof^{\mathrm{dec}}_{m,r}(K)
  =\Prof_{m,r}\bigl(\operatorname{Dec}_m(\operatorname{Sym}_mK)\bigr)
  \le
  \Prof_{m,r}\bigl(\operatorname{Dec}_mK\bigr).
\end{equation}
Consequently, for $p\ge2$ and $2\le r<\infty$,
\begin{equation*}
  \|I_m(K;W)\|_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r(\cC,\cE))}
  \le m^{m/2}C_m(p+r)^{m/2}
  \Prof_{m,r}\bigl(\operatorname{Dec}_mK\bigr).
\end{equation*}

