[Lemma lem:MP of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] Let $(x_0,s)\in\mathbb{R}^2$, and let $f$ be a continuous initial condition satisfying $f(x) \le a + b|x|$ for some constants $a,b >0$. Assume that $\mathcal{L}$ satisfies the metric composition property of the directed landscape, as well as the modulus of continuity bounds in Lemma (lem:Landscape_global_bound of the paper). Let $\mathfrak{h}_t(x):=\mathfrak{h}_t(x,f,s)$ be the KPZ fixed point solution at time $t$ with initial data $f$, and for ${\scaleobj{0.9}{\boxempty}} \in \{-,+\}$, let $\tau^{{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_t := \tau_{f;(x_0,s)}^{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}(t)$ be the interface defined as in (equation eq:taupm_def of the paper). Then, for any $s<r<t$,
            \begin{equation}
                \tau_t^{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}} =\tau^{{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{\mathfrak{h}_r;(\tau^{{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{r},r)}(t).
            \end{equation}

