[Lemma lem:modified_reflection_equations of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] Consider the set of equations
    \begin{align}
    w_1(t) &= b_1 + y_1(t) - c(t)\int_0^t\phi(w_1)(s)ds + \int_0^t\langle \iota, \xi_2(s)\rangle ds\\
    \langle f, \xi_2(t)\rangle &= \langle f, \gamma\rangle + \langle f, \alpha(\psi(w_1)(t))\rangle + \langle f, \beta(t)\rangle - \int_0^t \langle f\times \iota, \xi_2(s)\rangle ds ,
\end{align}
for all $f\in \Lipbar{\mathbb{R}, L}(\mathbb{S})$, where $b_1\in \mathbb{R}_-$, $\gamma\in \mathcal{M}_f$, $y_1\in \mathbb{D}_\mathbb{R}[0,\infty)$, $c\in \mathbb{G}_{\bar{\mathbb{S}}}[0,\infty)$,  $\alpha\in \Lip{\mathcal{M}_f, L}[0,\infty)$ and $\beta\in \mathbb{D}_{\mathcal{M}_s}[0,\infty)$ are given such that $|\alpha|_{TV,t}^*<\infty$ and $|\beta|_{TV,t}^*<\infty$ for all $t\geq 0$. Then (equation eq:reflected_equation1 of the paper)-(equation eq:reflected_equation2 of the paper) has a unique solution $(w_1, \xi_2)\in \mathbb{D}_{\mathbb{R}\times\mathcal{M}_s}[0,\infty)$.

