[Lemma 24 (Trace norm and Bures–Wasserstein distance) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] \label[lemma]{lem:gp-bures}
For positive trace-class operators $A$ and $B$ 
    \begin{equation}
    \norm{A-B}_1
    \le \{\sqrt{\tr(A)}+\sqrt{\tr(B)}\}
    \sd_{\rm BW}(A,B),
    \end{equation}
where $\|\cdot\|_1$ denotes the Schatten-1 norm and $\sd_{\rm BW}$ does the Bures–Wasserstein distance defined as
    \begin{align*}
    \sd_{\rm BW}^2(A,B)
    :=\tr(A+B-2(A^{1/2}BA^{1/2})^{1/2}).
    \end{align*}

