[Proposition Block graph event the for the one-arm event of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[proposition]{prop:block_one_arm}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel.  

    Then

    \begin{multline}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            o 
            \leftrightarrow 
            B(r)^c, 
            \# K
            \leq 
            k(r)
        \right) 
        \\
        \leq 
        \sum_{\substack{
            b \in \mathbf{N}
            \\
            \mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b)
            \\
            \mathbf{r} \in \mathcal{R}(b,\mathbf{m},r)
            \\
            \mathbf{A} \in \mathcal{A}(b,\mathbf{m})
        }}
        \sum_{\substack{
            \ell \in \mathbf{N}
            \\
            \mathbf{B} \in \mathcal{A}'(\ell,\mathbf{A})
        }}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            \mathcal{B}(K)
            =
            \mathbf{A} \cup \mathbf{B},
            P(\mathbf{A}, \mathbf{r}) 
            \subseteq 
            \mathcal{H}^*(\mathbf{A}),
            \mathbf{A} 
            \text{ is } 
            \mathcal{B}(K) 
            \text{-isolated}
        \right).
    \end{multline}

