[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2608.10515, 'Limiting Law of Local Fields for the Mean Field Ghatak-Sherrington Model'] Under the same conditions as in Proposition~\ref{prop:ratio}, we have
\begin{equation}
  \E\left[\langle U(l)\rangle-\frac{\E_\xi[U(\xi+\gamma)W(\beta(\xi+\gamma)+h)]}{\Wtil(\beta\gamma+h)}\right]^{2k}\le \frac{K}{N^k},
\end{equation}
where now $\xi\sim N(0,v)$ and $v=p-q$. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
  \frac{\E_\xi[U(\xi+\gamma)W(\beta(\xi+\gamma)+h)]}{\Wtil(\beta\gamma+h)}
  =\int U(x)d\nu_N(x),
\end{equation}
where $d\nu_N$ is the mixture of $2S+1$ Gaussian measures defined in \eqref{eq:nu-def}.

[Prop 1 of arXiv:2606.17472, '2606.17472'] Assume that $X$ is recurrent and (\ref{ConditionA}) holds. We have that there is a unique probability measure $\mu_B$ with support in $B$ that arises as the weak limit
  \begin{align*}
    r_q(0)m_B^q\Rightarrow \mu_B,\qquad q\to 0;
  \end{align*}
and a real-valued constant $k(B),$ such that
\begin{align*}
  \lim_{q\to 0}r_q(0)\Big(r_q(0)m_B^q(B)-1\Big)=k(B).
\end{align*} We will refer to $\mu_B$ as the  \emph{equilibrium measure} and to $k(B)$ as the \emph{Robin constant}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

