[Theorem cor of arXiv:2411.01731, '$L^2$-Wasserstein contraction of modified Euler schemes for SDEs with high diffusivity and'] Assume that $(i)$ $({\bf A}_0)$ with $\ell_0=0$, $({\bf A}_{4})$ and $({\bf A}_{5})$ with $\ell_0^\star=0$ for the EM scheme (equation WW of the paper);   $(ii)$ $({\bf A}_0)$, $({\bf A}_2)$ and $({\bf A}_{3})$ for the TEM scheme (equation EW0- of the paper);   $(iii)$ $({\bf A}_0)$, $({\bf A}_{4})$ and $({\bf A}_{5})$ for the PEM scheme (equation EWW of the paper). Then, there exist constants $C_0,\sigma_0,\lambda>0, \delta_2^{\star}\in(0,1]$ such that for all  $\delta\in(0,\delta_2^{\star}]$,   $\mu\in \mathscr P_2(\mathds R^d)$, and the noise intensity $\sigma$ satisfying $|\sigma|\ge\sigma_0,$
\begin{align}
\mathbb{W}_{2}\big(\pi_\8,\pi_\8^{(\delta)}\big)\le  C_0 \delta^{ \gamma_\star}  d^{\ell_\star},
\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\mathbb{W}_2(\mu P^{(\delta)}_{n\delta},\pi_\8)\le C_0 \big(\text{\rm{e}}^{-\lambda n\delta}	\mathbb{W}_2(\mu,\pi_\8)+\delta^{\gamma_\star}d^{\ell_\star}\big),
\end{align}
where $\pi_\8$ $($resp. $\pi_\8^{(\delta)}$$)$ is the unique IPM  of $(X_t)_{t\ge0}$ $($resp. $(X_{n\delta}^{\delta})_{n\ge0}$$)$, and
 $\gamma_\star=1,\ell_\star=1/2$  for the EM scheme (equation WW of the paper); $\gamma_\star=\gamma, \ell_\star=\ell_0+1/2$ for the TEM scheme (equation EW0- of the paper); $\gamma_\star=1,\ell_\star=(\ell_0+1+{\ell_0^\star}/2)\vee((\ell_0+1)/2+\ell_0/\gamma)$ for the PEM scheme (equation EWW of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2506.18132, 'Throughput in inhomogeneous planar drainage networks'] For all \(j \in \{0, 1\}\) and \(\alpha \in \big(1/2, 2/3\big) \), we have that
