[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] Let $a\in[1/2,1]$. Then for all $r\in[0,1]$,
\begin{equation*}
    \Beta\left(\frac{r}{1+r};a,a\right)\le \frac{r^a}{a}.
\end{equation*}

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:5f1619abcecc4237982544af5544a022d28a22aeaa064c5c018efc26c65b72f9","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/5f/5f1619abcecc4237982544af5544a022d28a22aeaa064c5c018efc26c65b72f9.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:05f32c6a14012228d1a6f5c4a03a590dfa205bbc605ef032ca359d8bc9ecc16d","bundle_entry_key":"2606-14876-lemma-31-beta-upper","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_050","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_050.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-14876-lemma-31-beta-upper","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Substituting $t=\frac{u}{1+u}$, we obtain
\begin{equation*}
    \Beta\left(\frac{r}{1+r};a,a\right) = \int_0^{\frac{r}{1+r}} t^{a-1}(1-t)^{a-1}\dif t = \int_0^r u^{a-1} \left(1+u\right)^{-2a}\dif u.
\end{equation*}
Note that for $u\in [0,r]$, $\left(1+u\right)^{-2a}\leq 1$. Hence we obtain
\begin{equation*}
    \Beta\left(\frac{r}{1+r};a,a\right) = \int_0^r u^{a-1} \left(1+u\right)^{-2a}\dif u \leq \int_0^r u^{a-1} \dif u = \frac{r^a}{a}.
\end{equation*}
