[Lemma lm:fourier-ball of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] We have 
\begin{align*}
 \widehat{ 1_{ B_{ 1}}}(u)  = \kappa _{ d}  \mathcal J_{ d/2}(\|u\|)
\end{align*}
with the renormalised Bessel function of the first kind 
\begin{align*}
 \mathcal J_{ \nu }(t) = \sum_{k = 0}^{ \infty }(-1)^{ k}a_{ k}(t),\qquad a_{ k}(t) = \frac{ 1}{k!\Gamma (k + \nu  + 1)}\left(
\frac{ t}{2}
\right)^{ 2k},
\end{align*} recalling $ \kappa _{ d} = \Leb(B_{ 1}) =  \widehat{ 1_{ B_{ 1}}}(0).$ It implies in particular by  [specialFunctionsBesselSec9.2]\begin{align*}
 \widehat{ 1_{ B_{ 1}}}(u) =c_{ d} \|u\|^{ -\frac{ d + 1}{2}}\sin(\|u\|-c'_{ d})(1 + o (1)),\qquad u\to \infty ,
\end{align*}
for some $ c_{ d},c'_{ d}>0,$
and
\begin{align}

 |  \widehat{ 1_{ B_{ 1}}}(u) |   = O((1 + \|u\|)^{ -\frac{ d + 1}{2}}).
\end{align} Also, we have the inequality
\begin{align}

 | \widehat{ 1_{ B_{ 1}}}(u) | \geqslant \frac{ \kappa _{ d}}{2}1_{ B_{ \rho _{ d}}}(u)
\end{align}where $ \rho _{ d} = { \sqrt{d + 2}} $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma le:beta-quotient-regimes of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ n \in {\mathbb N} $, $ \beta \in [0,1) $.
Then one has that
\bas{
\frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n}\le \begin{cases} \frac{2}{n}, & \text{ if } n\le (1-\beta)^{-1}\\
\frac{1-\beta}{1-e^{-1}}, & \text{ if } n\ge (1-\beta)^{-1}
\end{cases}
}

