[Lemma lhs of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Let $(X_1,d_1)$ and $(X_2,d_2)$ be two complete and locally compact metric spaces, and consider $f:(X_1,d_1)\to(X_2,d_2)$ a surjective map for which there exists $C>0$ and $\alpha>0$  such that for all $x,y \in X_1$, we have that
    \begin{equation*}
        d_2(f(x),f(y)) \leq Cd_1(x,y)^{\alpha}.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, we have that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \dim_H(X_2)\leq \frac{1}{\alpha} \dim_H(X_1).
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 8 (Coefficient asymptotics at an exponential singularity) of arXiv:2607.07712, 'Parameter-Space Heat Flow, Gaussian Density Ratios, and Sharp Hermite Truncation Rates'] Let \(\beta>0\) and \(\lambda>0\). Then, as \(m\to\infty\),
\begin{equation}
[z^m]\,
(1-z)^{-\beta}
\exp\!\left(
\frac{\lambda z}{1-z}
\right)
\sim
\frac{1}{2\sqrt\pi}\,
\lambda^{\frac14-\frac\beta2}\,
m^{\frac\beta2-\frac34}
\exp\!\left(
2\sqrt{\lambda m}-\frac{\lambda}{2}
\right).

\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:chi-properties of arXiv:2609.00840, 'Kählerity of complete almost-Kähler gradient shrinking Ricci solitons'] Let $(M^{2m},g,J,\omega,f)$, $m\geq2$, be a complete almost-K\"ahler gradient shrinking Ricci soliton.
	Then, for the star-Ricci form $\rho^{\ast}$ and the Ricci form $\rho$ defined in (equation eq:rho* of the paper) and (equation eq:ricci-form of the paper), respectively,
	\begin{equation}
		\rho^{\ast}=\rho+\frac12\nabla^{\ast}\nabla\omega.
	\end{equation}
	Moreover, the two-form $\chi$ defined in (equation eq:chi-def of the paper) is closed and satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\Lambda\chi:=\langle\chi,\omega\rangle=-\frac12|\nabla\omega|^2,
		\qquad
		\chi(V,W)=0,
	\end{equation}
	where $V=\nabla f$ and $W=JV$.

