[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] There is a constant $\rho>0$ such that for any integer $k\in[N(\log N)^{-1},N/2]$ and any $h\le\sqrt{\log N}$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P[0\connect{\varphi_N\ge h}\partial B_k]\lesssim\widetilde \eta_{N,k}^{h,\rho},
    \end{equation}
    where
    $$\wt\eta_{N,k}^{h,\rho}:=\begin{cases}
        \frac{|h|\vee\sqrt{\log N-\log k}}{\sqrt{\log N}},&h\le 0;\\
        \sqrt{\frac{\log N-\log k}{\log N}}\exp\left(-\frac{\rho h^2}{\log N-\log k}\right), &h>0.
    \end{cases}$$

