[Proposition 22 (Exponential-tail anisotropic estimates imply a subspace law) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Let $K\Subset\C\setminus[-b,b]$.  Suppose that, conditionally on $P_n$ when the signal is random, there are deterministic $a_n(K)\downarrow0$ and constants $C_K,c_K>0$ such that, for every deterministic unit $x,y\in\F^{2r_n}$ and every $t\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\left(
   \sup_{\zeta\in K}
   \left|\ip{x}{\bigl(\calG_n(\zeta)-\calM(\zeta)\bigr)y}\right|
   >a_n(K)+t
   \ \middle|\ P_n
 \right)
 \le C_K e^{-c_Knt^2}+e^{-c_Kn}.
\end{equation}
Then \cref{ass:holo-SLL} holds with
\begin{equation}
  \eps_n(K)\le C_K'
  \left(a_n(K)+\sqrt{\frac{r_n}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}\right).
\end{equation}
In particular, the error vanishes for every $r_n=o(n)$.

[Proposition prop:bd-Delta of arXiv:2411.11429, 'Functional Central Limit Theorem for topological functionals of Gaussian critical points'] Let $ A\subseteq \mathbb R^d$  {convex}, $ B\subseteq \mathbb R^{ d},r = 1 + d(A,B).$
For $ | \alpha | \le 3$,  { $ \partial _{ \alpha }\Delta _B$ satisfies (equation eq:scale-GFs-concentration of the paper)  with $ \sigma ^2 $ of the form $c r^{ d-2\eta }$, and $ \lambda $ depending on $ q$, hence} there is finite $ c>0$ depending on $ \alpha ,q,d$ such that for $ t\geqslant 0$
\begin{align*}
\mathbf P(\|\partial _{\alpha }\Delta _ B\|_A>t)\le c(1 +  \text{\rm{diam}}(A)^d)\exp\left(-\frac{ct^2}{(1+d(A,B))^{-2\eta +d }}\right).
\end{align*}

