[Theorem thm:nqthm1a0 of arXiv:2608.18990, 'Proving Lehner's formulas via RDT -- indefinite and asymmetric scenarios'] Assume the setup of Theorem (thm:thm1a0 of the paper) with $A_0\neq 0$. One then has  
\begin{eqnarray}

\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_a  
 \geq 
 \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E}  
    \max_{\substack{Y\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times k_1}, Y^TY =I\\ X\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times k_2}, X^TX =I}} \left ( \varphi + \sum_{i=1}^{l}  \mbox{Tr}\left ( G_i^{(4)} Y F_{i,Y}F_{i,Y}^T \right )  + \sum_{i=1}^{l} \mbox{Tr}\left ( G_i^{(5)} X F_{i,X}F_{i,X}^T \right )  \right )   .
\end{eqnarray}

