[Proposition prop:globalremainderest of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] Let $u$ be a URD solution to (equation eq:modeleqn of the paper). Then $R^u\in C^{\frac{1}{2\alpha}\textrm{-var}}([0,T]; H^{-2})$. Moreover:
    \begin{equation*}
        \left\| R^u \right\|_{C^{\frac{1}{2\alpha}\textrm{-var}}([0,T];H^{-2})}^{\frac{1}{2\alpha}}
         \lesssim  
        \left(1+ \left\| u \right\|_{L_T^\infty H}^{\frac{1}{2\alpha}}\right) \left[ \omega_\mu^{\frac{1}{2\alpha}}(0,T) +\omega_A(0,T) \right]+
        \frac{T^{3/2}}{\tilde{L}} \omega_u^{\frac 12}(0,T).
    \end{equation*}

