body:
[Theorem theorem_convergenceofpearsondiff of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Consider  the Pearson diffusion  (equation sde_pearson of the paper) with $b(y)=b_2y^2+b_1y+b_0>0,\forall y\in \mathbb{R}$. Assume $Z_t,t\geq 0$ is its non-stationary solution and $\mathcal{Z}$ is a random variable distributed as its stationary measure. Then $Z_t$ and $\mathcal{Z}$ admit infinitely differentiable densities and in particular, there exists a constant $c>0$ such that for any $k\in \mathbb{N}$ and $x\in (\ell,u)$, 
  \begin{align*}
       \abs{ p^{(k)}_{Z_t^{z_0}}(x)- p^{(k)}_{\mathcal{Z}}(x)}\leq C(x)\sqrt{z_0^2+1}e^{-ct}. 
    \end{align*}

