[Definition 8 of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] For $A\in\mathcal H_E$, define the multiplication-by-$t$ map
$\mathsf S_t:\mathcal H_E\to\mathcal H_E$ by
\begin{equation}
 K_{\mathsf S_t(A)}(x,y)=t(x,y)K_A(x,y).

\end{equation}
The right side is again an invariant bundle kernel.  On the
$\Omega$-isotypic summand, the induced map is
\begin{equation}
 \Theta_\Omega(A)=z_\Omega\mathsf S_t(A)z_\Omega.

\end{equation}

[Proposition 43 (Completed same-field Wick map) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Fix $2\le r<\infty$.  The map $\operatorname{Dec}_m$ extends
isometrically from $\mathfrak W_{m,r}$ into
\[
  \mathfrak T_{m,r}
  (\cH_\C^{(1)},\ldots,\cH_\C^{(m)};\cC,\cE).
\]
For every $p\ge2$, the algebraic Wick map extends uniquely to
\begin{equation}

  \mathcal I_{m,p,r}:\mathfrak W_{m,r}
  \longrightarrow L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r(\cC,\cE))
\end{equation}
with
\begin{equation}

  \|\mathcal I_{m,p,r}(\mathbf K)\|_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
  \le m^{m/2}C_m(p+r)^{m/2}
  \|\mathbf K\|_{\mathfrak W_{m,r}}.
\end{equation}
For fixed $r$, the extensions are compatible across $p$.  More generally,
if $2\le r\le s<\infty$, $\mathbf K\in\mathfrak W_{m,r}$, and
$p,q\ge2$, then
\begin{equation}

  \mathcal I_{m,p,r}(\mathbf K)
  =\mathcal I_{m,q,s}(\iota^{\mathrm W}_{r,s}\mathbf K)
  \quad\text{in }L^0(\Omega;\cL(\cC,\cE)).
\end{equation}
At $p=r=2$,
\begin{equation}

  \|\mathcal I_{m,2,2}(\mathbf K)\|_{L^2(\Omega;\Sch_2)}
  =\sqrt{m!}\,\|\mathbf K\|_{\mathfrak W_{m,2}}.
\end{equation}

