body:
[Proposition th:main2 of arXiv:2609.01488, 'Stabilization by a background magnetic field: global well-posedness of the full compressib'] Assume $\mathbf n$ satisfies the Diophantine condition (equation Diophantine0 of the paper) and the initial data \\ $(\rho_0,\mathbf u_0,p_0,\mathbf h_0)\in H^{N}(\mathbb T^3)$ satisfying (equation xiajie-1 of the paper)-(equation chuzhixiaoyu0 of the paper). Let $M,N$ be two integers satisfying $M\geq r+1$ and $N> M+2(r+1)$. Suppose that $(\rho,\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)$ is a smooth solution to   the system (equation no-heat-mhd3 of the paper) on $\mathbb T^3\times[0,T_1)$ for some $T_1>0$. Then there is a positive constant $\epsilon$, depending only on $\|\rho_0\|_M$, $\|\rho_0\|_N$, $\mathbb T^3$, $|\mathbf n|$, $M$, $N$, $\mu$, $\lambda$, $\gamma$, $\bar P$, $\underline{\rho}^{-1}$, $\bar\rho$, $M_0$, $r$ and $c$, such that
\begin{align}
&\frac{2}{3}\underline{\rho}\leq\rho\leq\frac32\bar\rho,\ \ \text{in}\ \mathbb T^3\times[0,T_1),\\
&\sup_{t\in[0,T_1)}\|\rho\|^2_{M}\leq 2\|\rho_0\|_{M}^2,\\
&\sup_{\tau\in[0,t]}\|\rho\|^2_{N}\lesssim\|\rho_0\|^2_{N}\big(1+\epsilon t \big),\\
&\sup_{\tau\in[0,t]}\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|^2_M\lesssim \Big(t+\big(M_\rho\|(\mathbf u_0,p_0,\mathbf h_0)\|^2_M\big)^{-\frac{r+1}{N-M}}\Big)^{-\frac{N-M}{r+1}},\\
&\sup_{t\in[0,T_1)}\|(\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)\|^2_N+\int_0^{T_1}\|\mathbf u_t\|^2_{N-1}dt+\int_0^{T_1}\|\mathbf u\|_{N+1}^2dt\leq \epsilon,
\end{align}
for any $t\in[0,T_1), $ as long as
\begin{equation}\|(\mathbf u_0,p_0,\mathbf h_0)\|_N\leq\epsilon.\end{equation}

