body:
[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2606.06231, 'Sensitivity of SDE Solutions to Perturbations of the Diffusion and Drift'] Suppose we have $a_n,b_n\in[0,\infty)$, $T,\tau\in(0,\infty)$, and measurable $f_n:[0,T]\to[0,\infty)$, $n\in\mathbb{Z}^+$ that satisfy
    \begin{align}
        f_n(t)\leq   b_n+a_n\int_0^t e^{\tau s}f_{n-1}(s)ds
    \end{align}
    for all $n\in\mathbb{Z}^+$, $t\in[0,T]$, where $f_0\coloneqq 1$.  Then for all $t\in[0,T]$, and defining $b_0\coloneqq 1$, we have
\begin{align}
    f_n(t)\leq \sum_{j=0}^n \frac{\prod_{k=j+1}^n a_k}{(n-j)! \tau^{n-j}} b_j  e^{(n-j)\tau t} \,.
\end{align}

