[Lemma lem:Identify of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $\delta \in (0, 1/2]$. There exists a constant $c_0 > 0$, depending only on $m$ and $d$, such that for all $r < \delta n$, and all $\eta \in \mathrm{Macro}(\delta)$, we have  
    \begin{equation*}
        c_0 r^{(d-1)(m-1)} \leqslant \abs{\left\{\zeta \in \Omega_n \colon \left\lVert\zeta - \eta\right\rVert_1 \leqslant r/2\right\}} \leqslant (r+1)^{(d-1)(m-1)},
    \end{equation*}
    for all $n$ large enough.

