[Theorem 15 (Integrated Davies trick) of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] For any $q\in[1,\infty]$, denote by $q'$ its H\"older conjugate and let $0\leq V,W\in\ell^\infty(X),$ $I\subset \RR$. Then, for any $q$-norm with respect to any measure on $X$, we have 
\begin{multline*}
\left(
\fint_I \|VP_{2\tau}W\|_{q',q}^\frac{q}{2}\drm \tau 
\right)^\frac{2}{q}
=
\left(
\fint_I \|WP_\tau V\|_{q',q}^\frac{q}{2}\drm \tau 
\right)^{\frac{2}{q}}
\\
\leq 
\inf_{\omega\in\ell^\infty(X)}
\sup_{\supp V}\euler^{-\omega}
\sup_{\supp W}\euler^{\omega}
\left(
\fint_I
\|V P_\tau^\omega\|_{2,q}^q
\drm \tau
\right)^\frac{1}{q}
\left(
\fint_I
\|W P_\tau^{-\omega}\|_{2,q}^q
\drm \tau
\right)^\frac{1}{q}.
\end{multline*}

