body:
[Theorem 47 (Fixed-rank Laurent integrality) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every zero-framed knot $K$, every fixed $n\ge2$, and every $k\ge0$,
the formal Newton coefficient in \eqref{eq:formal-SU} satisfies
\begin{equation}
 H_k^{(n)}(K;q)\in\Z[q^{\pm1}].
\end{equation}
Equivalently, for every $r\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 J_r^{SU(n)}(K;q)=\sum_{k=0}^{r}
 \left(\prod_{i=0}^{k-1}\{r-i\}\{r+n+i\}\right)
 H_k^{(n)}(K;q),
\end{equation}
with unique Laurent-polynomial coefficients.

[Lemma lemma-aux-result of arXiv:2607.08187, 'Asymptotic behaviours of critical branching random walk in $\mathbb{R}^d$'] For any $\gamma\geq 0$ and $\mathbf{y} \in D_1$,
	\begin{align}
		V_{(\gamma, \infty)}(\mathbf{y})-\left(\gamma/{\mathcal{C}(\alpha)}\right)^{\frac{1}{\alpha}} = \mathbb{N}_\mathbf{y}\Big(e^{-\gamma \zeta^X}1_{\{M^{X,d}\geq 1\}}\Big).
	\end{align}

