[Lemma 9 (Tree-contraction on $U_r$) of arXiv:2608.14802, 'Dynamical Gibbs-non-Gibbs transitions for finite-alphabet models on trees'] Let $\lambda_G\in (\lambda,1)$. Then there exist constants $r_0>0$ and $t_*=t_*(\lambda_G)<\infty$ such that, for every $r\in (0,r_0)$, every $t\geq t_*$, every $k\in S$, and all 
$(v^{(1)},\dots,v^{(d)}),(w^{(1)},\dots,w^{(d)})\in (U_r)^d$, the following estimate holds
\begin{equation}
    \left\|G_t^{[k]}(v^{(1)},\dots,v^{(d)}) - G_t^{[k]}(w^{(1)},\dots,w^{(d)})\right\|_l\leq\lambda_G \max_{i\in\{1,\dots,d\}}\|v^{(i)}-w^{(i)}\|_l.
\end{equation}

