[Corollary cor:L of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let (asn:b of the paper) and (asn:sigma of the paper) hold. Let  $\chi\in\mathrm{Cut}_d$, $p\in[1,\infty)$, and let $X$ and $Y$ be two solutions to (equation eq:main of the paper). Then the map $f\mapsto\mathcal{J} f$ defined for $f\in\mathcal{C}^2({\mathbb{R}}^d; {\mathbb{R}}^d)$ by
    \begin{equ}
        (\mathcal{J} f )_t=\int_0^1\int_0^t\chi_{\rho}(X_r-Y_r)\nabla f\big(\theta X_r+(1-\theta)Y_r\big)\,dr\,d\theta
    \end{equ}
    extends as a continuous linear map from $\mathcal{C}^{\alpha+}({\mathbb{R}}^d; {\mathbb{R}}^d)$ to $\mathcal{C}^{1+(\alpha-1)H}([0,1]; L_p(\Omega; {\mathbb{R}}^{d\times d}))$, whose norm depends only on $\alpha,p,d,\lambda,H,\chi,\|\sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^5},C^X_{D, p}, C^X_{S, 2p}, C^Y_{D,p}, C^Y_{S, 2p}$.

