[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2506.14145, '\bf Global-in-time optimal control of stochastic third-grade fluids with additive noise'] Suppose that $\Tr\left((-\Delta)^{3-2\gamma} GG^{\ast}\right)<\infty$ for $\gamma\in(0,\frac12)$,  $\vb_0\in \Drm(\A^{\frac32})$ and $\fb\in\Lrm^2(\Omega;\Lrm^2(0,T;\dot{\Hb}^1(\Tb^2)))$. Then, there exists a unique solution $\vb$ to system \eqref{stochastic-third-grade-fluids-equations} in the sense of Definition \ref{def-Solution}. In addition, the solution $\vb\in\mathrm{L}^{p}(\Omega;\mathrm{L}^{\infty}(0,T;\Drm(\A^{\frac32})))$, $p\geq2$, and for any given $\hat{c}>0$
    \begin{align}
   \Eb\bigg[\exp\bigg\{\hat{c}\int_0^t\|\vb(s)\|^{2}_{\dot{\Hb}^3} \drm s \bigg\}\bigg] <+\infty,
\end{align}
for all $t\in[0,T]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 65 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For each $p \geq 2$ there is a constant $C_p > 0$ such that
\begin{align*}
\bbe \big[ |B_{s,t}|^p \big] \leq C_p |t-s|^{p/2}, \quad s,t \in [0,T].
\end{align*}

