body:
[Corollary 26 (Critical-scale consistency transfer) of arXiv:2608.26693, '2608.26693'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:spectral-bounds}, $w_p=O(1)$, $\tau_p=p\bar\tau$, and \eqref{eq:w-consistency}, the critical-scale estimator is consistent in the sense that
\begin{equation}
\widehat u_p-\frac{U_p}{p}
\xrightarrow{\mathbb P}0.
\end{equation}
If the stronger input $\widehat w_p-w_p\to0$ almost surely holds, then the convergence in \eqref{eq:u-consistency} is also almost sure.  For $g(x)=2\bar\tau(1-e^{-x/(2\bar\tau)})$, one has the dimension-free contraction bound
\begin{equation}
|g(x)-g(y)|\le|x-y|,
\qquad x,y\ge0.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:corrupted:lipschitz of arXiv:2609.02304, 'Bayes-Optimal BER and AUC: \\Estimation and Evaluation of Estimators'] For any
  $
    \bm{z} = (z_{1}, \dots, z_{n})
    \in [0, 1]^{n}
  $
  and
  $
    \bm{w} = (w_{1}, \dots, w_{n}) 
    \in [0, 1]^{n}
  $,
  we have
  \begin{align}

    \abs{
      \widehat{\mathrm{BER}^*}(\bm{w}) 
      - 
      \widehat{\mathrm{BER}^*}(\bm{z})
    }
    &\leq
    \frac{1}{2 \min \set{\theta, 1 - \theta}} 
    \sqrt{
      \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n 
      (w_i - z_i)^{2}
    }
    \text{,}
    \\

    \abs{
      \widehat{\mathrm{AUC}^*}(\bm{w}) 
      - 
      \widehat{\mathrm{AUC}^*}(\bm{z})
    }
    &\leq
    \frac{1}{\theta (1 - \theta)}
    \sqrt{
      \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n
      (w_i - z_i)^{2}
    }
    \text{.}
  \end{align}

