[Lemma lem:finite-time-poc of arXiv:2607.00149, '\bf Uniform-in-time Propagation-of-Chaos for\\ Stein Variational Gradient Descent'] Let Assumption~(ass:poc of the paper) hold. Then there exist constants $C_0,c_0<\infty$ such that, for any $R >0$, $N\ge 3$ and
all $t\ge 0$,

\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\,\left[\sup_{0\le s\le t} \mathsf{KSD}_\pi(\mu^N_s,\mu_s)\, \mathbf{1}_{\{\int \|x\|^2 \mu^N_0(dx) \le R\}}\right]
\le C_0 N^{-\beta/2}\exp\{c_0(1+R)\exp(c_0t)\}.
\end{equation}

