body:
[Thm herm_corner of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] Fix a positive integer $n$, let $\lambda \in \Sig_n$, and let $A$ be a random element of $\Her_n(F)$ distributed by the $K$-invariant measure with singular numbers $\lambda$. Then the singular numbers of its top-left $(n-1) \times (n-1)$ corner $A'$ are given by
    \begin{equation}
        \Pr(\SN(A') = \nu) = \sum_{\kappa \in \Sig_{n-1}} \frac{P_{\lambda/\kappa}(1;t) P_\kappa(t,\ldots,t^{n-1};t)}{P_\lambda(1,\ldots,t^{n-1};t)} \cdot \frac{ Q_{\nu/\kappa}(-1;t)P_\nu(t,\ldots,t^{n-1};t)}{P_\kappa(t,\ldots,t^{n-1};t) \Pi_t(-1;t,\ldots,t^{n-1})}
    \end{equation}
    where $t=-q^{-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

