[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2605.27818, 'Exponential decay of mass for inertial coalescing particles with Hamiltonian noise'] There exist positive constants $\vt_1$ and $\eta_1$ and positive constants $c_1,c_2$, and $c_*0$, independent of $\eta_1$ and $\vt_1$, such that for every $\al>0$, 
and every $\vt\in(0,\vt_1)$ and $\eta\in(0,\eta_1\wedge c_*\vt^2)$,
\begin{equation}
x\in F_{\eta,\vt}\;\Longrightarrow\;|\div g_\al(x)|\leq
c_1\,\frac{\al\,n^2(0)}{l(0)+\al}\,\vt,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
x\in G_{\eta,\vt}\;\Longrightarrow\;\div g_\al(x)\geq
c_2\,\frac{\al\,n^2(0)}{l(0)+\al}\,\vt^2.
\end{equation}

