[Proposition foliation-of-lumpable-kernels of arXiv:2412.08400, '\vspace{-1.0cm} Characterization of Exponential Families of \\ Lumpable Stochastic Matrice'] {wolfer2024geometric}}]

For any fixed $P^\flat_0 \in \mathcal{W}(\mathcal{X}, \mathcal{D})$,
\begin{equation*}
    \mathcal{W}_\kappa(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}) = \biguplus_{P \in \mathcal{L}(P^\flat_0)} \mathcal{J}(P),
\end{equation*}
\begin{equation*}
    \dim \mathcal{W}_\kappa(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}) = \left| \mathcal{E} \right| - \sum_{(x,x') \in \mathcal{D}} \left| \mathcal{S}_x \right| + \left| \mathcal{D} \right| - \left| \mathcal{X} \right|.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

