[Lemma lem:Fu_derivative of arXiv:2608.13452, 'Wasserstein stability of the zero cell of a Poisson hyperplane tessellation under directio'] Let $x\geq 0$ and $u\in S^{d-1}$.
    The map $y'\mapsto F_u(x,y')$ is differentiable at almost every $y'> 0$, in which case it satisfies
    \begin{align*}
        \partial_y\big|_{y=y'}F_u(x,y) 
        &=2  \int_{(S^{d-1})^2}  \langle u,v_2 \rangle  \operatorname{\1}_{\langle x u , v_1\rangle < \langle y' u , v_2\rangle}  \operatorname{\1}_{\langle u,v_2 \rangle > 0} \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} \Phi(v_1 , v_2).
    \end{align*}

