[Lemma lem:uniform_linearized_martingale of arXiv:2608.27313, 'A Finite Sample Analysis for Quantile Temporal Difference Learning in Distributional Reinf'] Let $n$ be an $({\mathcal{F}}_t)$-stopping time with $u\le n\le v$, and let
$\sigma\ge n$ be a stopping time such that
$\norm{\bm\theta^{(t)}-\bm\theta_m}_\infty\le r_{\mathrm{out}}$
on $\{t<\sigma\}$. For every $\eta\in(0,1)$,
conditionally on ${\mathcal{F}}_n$, with probability at least $1-\eta$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\max_{q\in{\mathcal{S}}\times[m]}\max_{n\le r<k\le T}
\abs{\sum_{t=r}^{k-1}\alpha_t\bm e_q^\top
{\bm{\Phi}}_{t+1,k}\mathbf{1}\{t<\sigma\}{\bm{\xi}}^{(t+1)}}\\
&\quad\le
2\sqrt{\frac{v_m\alpha_n}{1-\gamma}
\log\frac{2|{\mathcal{S}}|mT^2}{\eta}}
+\frac{\alpha_n}{3}\log\frac{2|{\mathcal{S}}|mT^2}{\eta}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

