[Theorem main result 3 of arXiv:2412.09850, 'Averaging principles for time-inhomogeneous multi-scale SDEs via nonautonomous Poisson equ'] Suppose that Assumptions {\rm(B1 of the paper)}, {\rm(A2 of the paper)} and {\rm(A4 of the paper)} hold, and $\sigma(x,y)=\sigma(x)$. Let $\{X_t^\varepsilon, Y_t^\varepsilon \}_{t\ge0}$ and $\{\bar X_t\}_{t\ge0}$ be the solutions of (equation Equation of the paper) and (equation AVE21 of the paper) respectively. Then, for any $T>0$ and $\beta\in(0,1)$, there exists a constant $C_{T,\beta}>0$ so that for $\varepsilon>0$,
\begin{align*}
\sup_{t\in [0, T]}\mathbb{E} |X_{t}^{\varepsilon}-\bar{X}_{t} |^2\leqslant  C_{T,\beta}(1 + |x|^2 + |y|^2)\varepsilon^2\Bigg\{&\left[\int_0^{T/\varepsilon}\left(\int^{s}_0 e^{-2\beta\alpha (s-r)}\phi^2(r)\,dr\right)^{1/2}\,ds\right]^2\\
&  +\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant T}|\Lambda_{\gamma}(t/\varepsilon)|^2  +  \int^{T/\varepsilon}_0     \alpha(s)\Lambda^2(s)\,ds\Bigg\}.
\end{align*}

