[Lemma lem:core of process of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $V$ be an  upper probability on a measurable space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$, and  $\textbf{Y}=\{Y_n\}_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a bounded stationary process on a capacity space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V)$. Then for any $\widetilde{P}\in \operatorname{core}(V_{\textbf{Y}})$, there exists  $P'\in\operatorname{core}(V)$ such that 
	\begin{equation}
		\widetilde{P}(C)=P'(\textbf{Y}^{-1}(C)) \text{ for any }C\in\sigma(\mathcal{C}).
	\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:stima_HS_1 of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Assume that there exists a positive constant $\delta$ such that 
\begin{align}

\mu_n\sim  n^{\delta}, \qquad \delta>\frac{1}{\alpha}.
\end{align}
Then, Hypothesis (hyp:base of the paper) are fulfilled, i.e.,  $e^{tA}G(\tau)\in\mathcal L_2(U;H)$ for every $t\in(0,T]$ and every $\tau\in[0,T]$, and there exist positive constants $C_G$ and  $\gamma_G\in\left(0,\frac12\right)$ such that (equation hyp_base1 of the paper) is satisfied. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

