[Definition 14 (Mild Integral Formulation) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] A mapping $u_\varepsilon \in \mathcal{B}_m([0, T] \times H)$ is defined as a \emph{mild solution} to the penalized backward equation \eqref{eq:hjb_penalized} if it satisfies the following integral equation on $[0, T] \times H$:
\begin{equation} 

    u_\varepsilon(t, x) = P_{t,T}[\Psi](x) + \int_t^T P_{t,s} \left[ f(s, \cdot) - \frac{1}{\varepsilon} \left( u_\varepsilon(s, \cdot) - \Phi(s, \cdot) \right)^+ \right](x) \, \mathrm{d}s.
\end{equation}

