[Theorem 40 (Conditional consistency of the minimal-window estimator) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Under \cref{ass:estimation}, define
\begin{equation}
\widehat m_n:=\min\Bigl\{1\le m\le M:\sigma_{\min}(\widehat J_{n,m})>\gamma\Bigr\},
\end{equation}
with the convention $\widehat m_n=M+1$ if the set is empty.
Then
\begin{equation}
\widehat m_n\to m_*(T,\theta_0) \qquad\text{in probability.}
\end{equation}

