{"artifact_digest":"sha256:a69e9d87242f18f65be06d1880522f98375db951bfc71d887801d7ba612d2f42","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/a6/a69e9d87242f18f65be06d1880522f98375db951bfc71d887801d7ba612d2f42.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:08649ca9deb4b13d2782beee35a150d57a40837f7b7ae18c900229e7ebb42540","bundle_entry_key":"2606-28031-lemma-0-characteristic-function-v","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_037","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_037.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-28031-lemma-0-characteristic-function-v","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Fix $t\geqslant 0$ and $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$. Let $n \in {\mathbb N}$ and define $t_k=\frac{k}{n}t$ for each $k\in{{\left\{0,\ldots,n\right\}}}$. Since $F$ is a bounded càdlàg process, by [protter04], we have
\begin{align*}
\int_{0+}^t F(s-) \, {\mathrm d} X(s) = \lim_{n \to \infty} \sum_{k=0}^{n-1} F(t_k) \PAR{X(t_{k+1})-X(t_k)} ,
\end{align*}
where the limit is \textit{uniformly on compacts in probability}. As a consequence, we have
\[
