[Lemma lemma_steinmethod_xmorethanu of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Fix $x\geq u$ and $k\in \mathbb{N}$. Let the function $h$ in the ODE (equation equation_stein of the paper) be 
    \begin{align*}
        h(y)=h_{k,x}(y):=\mathds{1}_{\{y> x\}}\rho_{k+1}(y), \qquad y\in  
         \{ y\in (x,\infty):b(y)=0\}. 
    \end{align*} 
Then the solution $g_{k,x}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ to (equation equation_stein_pearson of the paper) exists and satisfies for every $y\in \mathbb{R}$, 
\begin{align*}
     \abs{ g_{k,x}(y)}&\leq  \mathcal{U}_5(k,y):=\mathds{1}_{\{y>u\}} C\frac{\sum_{j=0}^{k+1} \left\vert y \right\rvert^j }{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert^{k+1}\left\vert y-m \right\rvert }
    \end{align*}
and
\begin{align*}
    \abs{ g'_{k,x}(y)}&\leq  \mathcal{U}_6(k,y)]]\\
    &:=\mathds{1}_{\{y>u\} } C\brac{\frac{\sum_{j=0}^{k+1} \left\vert y \right\rvert^j }{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert^{k+1}\left\vert y-m \right\rvert^2 } +\frac{\sum_{j=0}^{k} \left\vert y \right\rvert^j }{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert^{k+1}\left\vert y-m \right\rvert }+\frac{\left\vert b'(y) \right\rvert\sum_{j=0}^{k+1} \left\vert y \right\rvert^j }{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert^{k+2}\left\vert y-m \right\rvert }}. 
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

