body:
[Proposition prop: Bounds A-loc. states of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] Consider a nearest-neighbor $\mathbb{Z}_q$-valued clock model with Gibbsian specification defined via the transfer operator $Q(i)=e^{-\beta \overline{u}(i)}$ where the function $\overline{u}$ satisfies the $u,U,d$-condition (equation eq: u,U-bounds of the paper). Then, we have 
   \begin{equation}
    (q-1)^{\frac{2}{d+1}}e^{-\beta U}\leq\epsilon \leq (q-1)^{\frac{2}{d+1}}e^{-\beta u}.
\end{equation}
   Furthermore, let $ A \subset \mathbb{Z}_q$ with $n=|A|\geq 1$ and $\beta$ be large enough, then there exists a spatially homogeneous tree-indexed Markov chain Gibbs measure $\mu_A$ which is localized on the subset $A$. The transition matrix $P_A$ is strictly positive and the following bounds hold:  
   \begin{align*}
       (i) ~\|&\Delta|_{A^c}\|_{\frac{d+1}{d-1}}\leq C_1 e^{-(d-1)\beta u},~~~~(ii)~\min_{i\in A} \Delta(i)>1-C_2e^{-\beta u},\\
        (iii) ~\sum_{i\in A^c} \pi_A(i) \leq C_1&  e^{-(d+1)\beta u},~~~~(iv)~ \Big(1-(C_1+C_2)  e^{-\beta u} \Big) \frac{1}{|A|}\leq \pi_A|_A  \leq \left(1-C_2e^{-\beta u}\right)^{-1} \frac{1}{|A|}
   \end{align*}
   where $C_1:=2^{d+1}d^3(n+1)^{d}(q-1)^{2}$ and $C_2:=3d(d^{\frac{1}{d-1}}-1)(n+1)(q-1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 28 of arXiv:2603.05174, 'Regularization of the superposition principle: Potential theory meets Fokker-Planck equati'] If \eqref{eq:b da in L2 loc duplicate}, \eqref{eq:ellipticity_duplicate}, and \eqref{eq:hu in H-1} hold, then for every $\gamma\in(0,1)$ we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \int_0^N\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}h\frac{\|\nabla (hu)\|^2}{(hu)^\gamma}\;dxdt<\infty,\quad 0\leq h\in C_c^\infty((0,N)\times \mathbb{R}^d).
    \end{equation*}

