\end{equation}
If \(x\notin A_u\), the ratio is \(0\). Hence
\begin{equation}
\frac{\widetilde Q_{n-u,p}(x)}{U(x)}
=u!\,p^u\,\mathbf 1_{A_u}(x)
=u!\,p^u\,\mathbf 1_{\{L_p(x)\ge u\}}.
\end{equation}
