[Coro 32 of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] In the same context as Proposition \ref{proposition formula for en_J cap ber(1-p) (AF)}, fix $e\in E$. The function $q_e \mapsto \en_{J,p}(\A_F)$ is a M\"obius map. In particular, its derivative is of constant sign, and when $q$ and $p$ are related by the relation $p=1-q^2$, its sign is equal to the sign of \begin{equation}
\left(\sum_{\eta\in\F, e\not\in\eta}q_\eta\right)\left(\sum_{\eta\in\F, e\in\eta}q_{\eta\Delta F}\right)- \left(\sum_{\eta\in\F, e\in\eta}q_\eta\right)\left(\sum_{\eta\in\F, e\not\in\eta}q_{\eta\Delta F}\right),
\end{equation}
where $\F$ is a shorthand for the dual HT structure $\F_G^*$ on $G$.

