[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] Under $\mathbb Q_s$, let $U$ be the spine particle at time $s$, and let
$q_U(\mathcal T_s)$ be the conditional probability that one coordinate is
saturated by time $s$ and $U$ carries its least-saturated direction.  Then, for
every $\vartheta>1$,
\begin{equation}
 \E\!\left[\sum_{u\in V_s}\vartheta^{L_u}\right]
 \le d\,e^{-\lambda B}
 \E_{\mathbb Q_s}\!\left[
 e^{(\vartheta-1)dq_U(\mathcal T_s)}\right].
\end{equation}

