\[
  X(\gamma)=\sum_k\gamma_kB_k,
  \qquad
  f(\gamma)=\norm{X(\gamma)}_{\Sch_r}.
\]
The expectation bound \eqref{eq:self-adjoint-expectation-lipschitz} is
the Gaussian Schatten noncommutative Khintchine inequality at exponent $r$;
see Lust-Piquard--Pisier \cite{LustPiquardPisier}, Buchholz
\cite{Buchholz}, and Pisier \cite[Section~9.8]{PisierBook}.  Its
self-adjoint finite-dimensional specialization is
\begin{equation}

  \E f
  \le (\E f^r)^{1/r}
  \le C\sqrt r\,
  \biggl\|\biggl(\sum_kB_k^2\biggr)^{1/2}\biggr\|_{\Sch_r}.
\end{equation}
It remains to compute the Lipschitz constant.  For every scalar vector $a=(a_k)$,
\begin{equation}

