[Lemma l.rescaled_DeGiorgi of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Fix $z_0$.  Suppose $g$ is a weak solution to~(equation eq:linear_kinetic of the paper) in $Q_{2r}(z_0)$ with coefficients satisfying~(equation defn:coercivity_assumption of the paper)-(equation defn:bounded_coefficient_assumption of the paper). Suppose that $g \in L^\infty_m$ for some $m \in \mathbb R$.  Then there exists $\alpha\in (0,1)$, depending only on $\lambda, \Lambda$, such that
    \begin{equation}
        [g]_{C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_\frac{r}{2}(z_0))}
        \lesssim \frac{1}{r^\alpha \left\langle v_0 \right\rangle^{m - \frac{3\alpha}{2}}} \left\|g\right\|_{L^\infty_m(Q_{2r}(z_0))}.
    \end{equation}
    Recall that $\tilde r = r \left\langle v_0 \right\rangle^{-\nicefrac32}$ and $r = \min\{1, \nicefrac{\sqrt{t_0}}2\}$.

