[Lemma W1.1-1 of arXiv:2411.09949, '$W_{\bf d}$-convergence rate of EM schemes for invariant measures of supercritical stable '] Let $0<\eta<{\mathord{{\rm min}}}\{1,\frac{\kappa_1}{8\kappa_0^{2}},\frac{1}{\kappa_1}\}$ and $p\in(0,\alpha)$.
Then there is a unique invariant probability measure $\mu_{\eta}$ such that for all $k\geqslant1$, $p\in(0,\alpha)$ and $x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}|Y_{k}^{x}|^p\leqslant K V_{p}(x),
\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\sup_{\|f/V_{p}\|_{\infty}\leqslant 1}|\mathbb{E}f(Y_{k}^{x})-\mu_{\eta}(f)|\leqslant KV_{p}(x)e^{-\lambda k},
\end{align}
where $K, \lambda>0$ depend on $\alpha,d,\kappa_0,\kappa_1,\kappa_2$.

