[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2605.17494, 'Generalized intersection exponents and local cut points for three-dimensional Brownian loo'] For all $\alpha \in I_0$, the following holds almost surely:
    \begin{equation}
        {\rm dim}_{\mathcal{H}}(G) \le \max \{2-\xi_{\alpha}(1,1),0 \},
    \end{equation}
    and the following holds with positive probability
    \begin{equation}
        {\rm dim}_{\mathcal{H}}(G) \ge \max \{2-\xi_{\alpha}(1,1),0 \}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Defn def:I-s-iota-sharp of arXiv:2609.03751, 'Sparse bounds for maximal rough singular integrals'] For \(n=1\), set
\[
    \mathcal I_{s,\iota}^{\sharp,1}
    :=
    \left\{
      K\in\mathscr K_s^{\vec w}:
      K^\iota\nsubseteq F_{s,\iota}^1
    \right\}.
\]
For \(n\geq2\), set
\[
    \mathcal I_{s,\iota}^{\sharp,n}
    :=
    \left\{
      K\in\mathscr K_s^{\vec w}:
      K^\iota\subseteq F_{s,\iota}^{n-1}
      \ \text{and}\
      K^\iota\nsubseteq F_{s,\iota}^{n}
    \right\}.
\]

