[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Fast edges of the reduced graph $(\hat V, \hat E\,)$ coincide with fast edges of the original graph $(V,E)$ with both endpoints in $\hat V$, namely $\hat E_F=E_F[\hat V]\,$.

	Moreover, if $(x,y)\in \hat E_F$ necessarily both endpoints belong to the same minimal class $M\in\mathcal M$ and
\begin{equation} 
	\hat r_N(x,y) \,=\, r_N(x,y) \,(1+ o_N(1))\,,\quad (x,y)\in \hat E_F
\end{equation}
where $o_N(1)$ vanishes as $N\to\infty$.

[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2605.30055, 'The Wasserstein cost of importance sampling'] For any $Q \subset (0,1)^d$ and any fixed $p>0$, 

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}\left[ \left| \frac{\kappa_Q}{n} - 1 \right|^p\right] \les \mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\kappa_Q}{n}\right)^{p/2}.
    \end{equation}

