satisfies  $\beta> 1/2.$
Then,  there exists a   constant
$  C_0  >0$
such that for all
 $\delta\in(0,\delta_2^{\star\star}]$, $n\ge0,$ $\mu\in \mathscr P_2(\mathds R^d)$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{W}_{2}\big(\pi_\8,\pi_\8^{(\delta)}\big)\le  C_0 \delta^{1\wedge\beta}  d^{\frac{1}2\ell_\star}   ,
\end{equation}
  and
\begin{align}
\mathbb{W}_2(\mu P^{(\delta)}_{n\delta},\pi_\8)\le C_0 \big(\text{\rm{e}}^{-\frac{1}2(\lambda_1\wedge\lambda_2) n\delta}	\mathbb{W}_2(\mu,\pi_\8)+\delta^{1\wedge \beta}  d^{\frac{1}2\ell^\star}   \big),
\end{align}
where  $\pi_\8$ $($resp. $\pi_\8^{(\delta)}$$)$
is  the $($resp. unique$)$   IPM of $(X_t)_{t\ge0}$ $($resp. $(X_{n\delta}^\delta)_{n\ge0}$ determined by (equation E2 of the paper)$)$,
\begin{align}
\ell_\star:= \big(2\ell_0+1+(1+\ell_0^\star)\mathds 1_{\{\beta>\frac12\}}\big)\vee(\ell_0+l_2)\vee l_\beta^{*},~~   ~~ \delta_2^{\star\star}:=\delta_1^\star\wedge\big( K_R^*/(4\psi^2_2(1))\big)^{\frac{1}{1-2 \theta}},
\end{align}
and the quantities $\lambda_1,\lambda_2, \delta_1^\star>0$ were given in Theorem (thm of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2606.03122, 'Propagation of support for super-Brownian motion with general branching mechanism'] Suppose that $X$ is a super-Brownian motion with branching mechanism $\Psi$ satisfying Condition \ref{con_localize}. For any $\mu\in M_c$, there exists a positive constant $C(d)$ that depends only on the dimension $d$, such that for any $0\leq\rho(\mu)<R_1 < R$ and $t\in\left(0,\dfrac{(R_1-\rho(\mu))^2}{d}\right)$, we have
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\mathbb{P}_{\mu}\{\exists s\leq t,X_s(\overline{B(0,R)}^c)>0\}\\
&\quad\leq \mu(1)\cdot u_{R,\Phi_R}(R_1)\cdot C(d) \left(\dfrac{R_1-\rho(\mu)}{\sqrt{t}}\right)^{d-2}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(R_1-\rho(\mu))^2}{2t}\right)\\
&\quad\leq \mu(1)\cdot G_{\Phi_R}^{-1}(R-R_1)\cdot C(d) \left(\dfrac{R_1-\rho(\mu)}{\sqrt{t}}\right)^{d-2}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(R_1-\rho(\mu))^2}{2t}\right).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

