body:
[Lemma lem:ckreform of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] Consider the Crow-Kimura replicator-mutator equation 
	\begin{align}

		\partial_t \rho_t(x) = - \nabla \cdot (\rho_t(x) g(x)) + \frac{1}{2} \nabla \cdot (\Sigma \rho_t(x))  +  \rho_t(x) (\mathbb{E}_{z \sim \rho_t}[f_t(x,z)] -  \mathbb{E}_{\rho_t}[f_t]) 
	\end{align}
	with fitness landscape given by (equation eq:genquadfit of the paper).  This equation can be expressed in the form 

	\begin{align}
		\nonumber 
		\partial_t \rho_t(x) = \mathcal{L}^\ast \rho_t(x) +  (r-s) &\left( - \frac12\left( h(x)^\top\Xi^{-1} h(x)   - \mathbb{E}_{\rho_t}[h^\top\Xi^{-1} h]\right) + \left(h(x) - \mathbb{E}_{\rho_t}[h] \right)^\top\Xi^{-1}\frac{dZ_t^d}{dt} \right)\rho_t(x) \\

		-\frac{s}{2} &\left( \| h(x) - \mathbb{E}_{\rho_t}[h] \|_\Xi^2  - \mathbb{E}_{\rho_t}\left[\| h(x) - \mathbb{E}_{\rho_t}[h] \|_\Xi^2 \right] \right) \rho_t(x). 
	\end{align}
	where $\mathcal{L}^\ast$ denotes the adjoint of the generator of the diffusion process (equation eq:sig of the paper).  Additionally, the unnormalised form is given by 
	\begin{align}

		\partial_t \mu_t(x) = \mathcal{L}^\ast \mu_t(x) +  \left(   - \frac{r}{2} h(x)^\top\Xi^{-1} h(x) +  (r-s) h(x)^\top \Xi^{-1}\frac{dZ_t^d}{dt}  \right) \mu_t(x) 
	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 44 of arXiv:2606.17859, 'Full $\Gamma-$expansion for the level-two large deviation rate functionals of non-reversib'] There exists a finite constant $C_0 = C_0(\mf q, \mtt a(\cdot))$ such
that
\begin{equation*}
\sup_{x\in \bb T}
\bb E_{x}^{\epsilon} [\, \tau (\mc M_p) \, ]
\,\le\, C_0 \, \epsilon^{-1}\, e^{\mf h_{p-1}/\epsilon}
\end{equation*}
for all $1\le p\le \mf q$, provided $\mf h_0=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

