[Lemma covougff of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Take $(e_n)_{n\in \mathbb N}$ an orthonormal basis of $H_0^1(D)$ with the inner product of (equation eq.h01-ip of the paper) to define the OU-GFF $\varphi$. Then, the collection $(\langle \varphi(t), f\rangle_\nabla)_{t\in \mathbb R, f\in H_0^1(D)}$ is a centered Gaussian process with covariance given by
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb E[\ipn{\varPhi(t)}{f} \ipn{\varPhi(s)}{g}] 
        = e^{-\frac{1}{2}|s-t|}\ipp{f}{g}_{\nabla}, \ \ \ \text{ for any $s,t \in R$ and $f,g \in H_0^1(D)$.} 
    \end{equation}
    As a consequence, for $f,g\in H_0^{-1}(D)$  and $s,t\in \mathbb R$
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb E[\ipp{\varPhi(t)}{f}\ipp{\varPhi(s)}{g}] = 
        \frac{1 }{2\pi } e^{-\frac{1}{2}|t-s|}\ipp{f}{(-\Delta)^{-1}g},
    \end{equation*}
     thus the law of $\varPhi$ does not depend on the choice of the basis $(e_n)_{n\in \mathbb N}$.

