{"artifact_digest":"sha256:3133d1ebf62ac030c694f35c4caa535aeb353cc2f6d88f1cf477d60ca4b7315d","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/31/3133d1ebf62ac030c694f35c4caa535aeb353cc2f6d88f1cf477d60ca4b7315d.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:8ac09ae97b6566efe34f22ef92aebc940dc903be796fc711bfa0e9f450fd3014","bundle_entry_key":"2606-11043-lemma-14-covougff","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_031","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_031.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-11043-lemma-14-covougff","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We start by noting that \begin{align*}
    \langle \varphi(t), f\rangle_\nabla = \sum_{k\in \mathbb N} \alpha_k(t) \langle e_k, f\rangle_{\nabla}.
