[Theorem 5 (Least jump fixed point) of arXiv:2608.25925, '\textbf{Jump Closure and Limit Uniformization\\in the Ideal Completion of the Turing Degre'] Starting from $\down\mathbf a$, the finite iterates of $\Gamma$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
\Gamma^n(\down\mathbf a)=\down\mathbf a^{(n)}

\end{equation}
for every $n<\omega$, and
\begin{equation}
\lfp_{\geq\down\mathbf a}(\Gamma)
=
\bigcup_{n<\omega}\down\mathbf a^{(n)}
=
\operatorname{Arith}(\mathbf a).

\end{equation}
The closure ordinal of this iteration is exactly $\omega$.

