[Lemma lem:vd-l2-layer-hessian of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Let $\phi$ solve (equation eq:vd-l2-poisson-problem of the paper). Then
\begin{align}

 \abs{
 \int_{\Omega\times\mathbb S^1}
 \mathcal U_{\rm sl,0}^\varepsilon(x,w)
 (w\otimes w):D_x^2\phi(x)
 \,\mathrm d x\mathrm d\nu(w)
 }
 &\leq
 C_\Omega\mathcal G_{\rm vd}
 \left(
 \varepsilon^{\frac12}
 +\sum_{m:\,\omega_m>\pi}
 \varepsilon^{\lambda_{m,1}}
 \right)
 \nm{\varrho}_{L^2(\Omega)}
 \leq
 C_\Omega\mathcal G_{\rm vd}\varepsilon^{\frac12}
 \nm{\varrho}_{L^2(\Omega)}.
\end{align}

[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] There exists $C \equiv C(T,k,A,\lVert u \rVert_{L^\infty_{x}}, \gamma, d,p)>0$ such that for any $N\in \N^*$,
\begin{align*}
\big\| u_t^{(N)} - u_t \big\|_{ \gamma,p}
\leq C \int_{0}^t \frac{1}{(t-s)^{\tilde{\gamma}}} \Big( \big\| u_s^{(N)} - u_s \big\|_{ \gamma,p} +  \big\| \langle v \rangle^{k} (F^{(N)}_{s}-F_{s}) \big\|_{L^{2}_{x,v}} \Big) \dd s ,
\end{align*}
where $\tilde{\gamma}\in (0,1)$ is defined in \eqref{eq:deftildegamma}.

