body:
[Lemma L:basic-stationary-est of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Fix $\alpha_0 \in (0, 1/2)$. There is $c>0$ depending only on $\alpha_0$ such that the following is true. Take parameters $\alpha, \beta$ such that $\alpha > \alpha_0$, $\beta \in (2(1/2 - \alpha)\vee 0, 1/2 - \alpha_0)$. Set
$$
\bar Z^+(i) =\begin{cases}
	Z^+(i) - \frac{i}{1/2 - \beta}, \qquad i \ge 0 \\
	Z^+(i) - \frac{|i|}{1/2 + \beta}, \qquad i < 0.
\end{cases}
$$
 Then for any $i < j \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $m > 0$ we have that
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{P}\Big(\max_{r < s \in \llbracketi,j \rrbracket} |\bar Z^+(s) - \bar Z^+(r)| \ge m\Big) \le 2\exp \left(-\frac{cm^2}{m + (j - i)} \right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $j_0 \in \mathbb{Z}, \delta > 0,$ and $m > 0$ we have that
\begin{equation}

	\mathbb{P}(|\bar Z^+(j_0 + i) - \bar Z^+(j_0)| \le m + \delta i^2 \text{ for all } i \in \mathbb{Z}) \ge 1 - 2\exp \left(-\frac{cm^2}{m + \sqrt{m/\delta}} \right).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

