[Thm general-local-thm of arXiv:2509.07729, 'Permuton and local limits for the Luce model'] Set $f_n(y):=\theta_{\lfloor yn \rfloor}$ for all $y\in[0,1]$ and assume that $f_n\to f$ almost everywhere for some positive, finite, measurable function $f$ on $[0,1]$. 
Then, for all $k\geq 1$ and every permutation $\pi\in\mathcal{S}_k$,
\begin{equation}
    \Lambda(\pi)=\lim_{n\to +\infty}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=0}^{n-k}p\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(\theta_{i+\pi^{-1}(1)},\dots, \theta_{i+\pi^{-1}(k)}\aftergroup\egroup\originalright)=\frac{1}{k!},
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{(\nu_n(\pi))^2}{n}=\nu_\infty(\pi),
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{equation}
\nu_\infty(\pi)
=\frac{1}{k!}+\frac{1-2k}{(k!)^2}+2 \sum_{h=1}^{k-1}\zeta_{\pi}(h,k),
\end{equation}
with
\begin{equation}
    \zeta_{\pi}(h,k):=\mathbb P\!\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(
E_{\pi^{-1}(1)}<\dots<E_{\pi^{-1}(k)},
\;\; E_{h+\pi^{-1}(1)}<\dots<E_{h+\pi^{-1}(k)}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright),\quad\text{$1\le h\le k-1$,}
\end{equation}
where $(E_{j})_{j}$ are i.i.d.\ exponential random variables with parameter 1. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

