[Theorem thm:liftedPoincare of arXiv:2607.10801, 'Relaxation times of non-reversible\\ Markov processes'] Let $(\mathcal{E},\dom(\mathcal{E}))$ be a densely defined, closed, non-negative definite symmetric bilinear form on $L_0^2(\mu)$, and let $({\mathcal{C}},\dom({\mathcal{C}}))$ be the non-positive self-adjoint linear operator on $\mathbb{H}^l$ that is the generator of $\mathcal{E}$ restricted to $\mathbb{H}^l$.
    Assume that there are constants $m,C\in (0,\infty)$ with
    \begin{align}\tag{B}
        \mathcal{E}(g,g)\ &\geq\ m\norm{g}^2&&\kern-2em\text{for all }g\in \dom(\mathcal{E})\cap\mathbb{H}^l\,,\\
        \mathcal{E}(f,g)\ &\leq\ C\norm{f}\norm{{\mathcal{C}}g}&&\kern-2em\text{for all }f\in\dom(\mathcal{E})\cap\mathbb{H}^h,\, g\in\dom({\mathcal{S}})\,.\tag{C}
    \end{align}
    Then
    \begin{equation}
        \norm{f}^2\ \leq \ \frac{2}{m}\mathcal{E}(f,f)\ +\ (1+2C^2)\norm{f-\Pi f}^2
    \end{equation}
    for all $f\in\dom(\mathcal{E})$ with $\Pi f\in\dom(\mathcal{E})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

