[Lemma 11 (Endpoint estimate in a mixed strip) of arXiv:2608.30304, '2608.30304'] Let $n\ge1$, $\alpha\ge A_0$ and $-\tfrac12\le\beta\le A_0$. If
\begin{equation}
0\le 1+x\le\rho_{n,\alpha}:=\frac2{(n+1)(n+\alpha+1)},
\end{equation}
then, with $S=\alpha+\beta+1$,
\begin{equation}
 F_{n,\alpha,\beta}(x)\le22\,\mathcal E_n(S).
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:mixed_tail_measurability of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] For every $j\in\cbr{1,2}$, the map
\begin{align*}
(t,r)\longmapsto\mu_j(B_{d_j}(t,r))
\end{align*}
is Borel measurable on $T\times[0,\infty)$. Consequently,
$v_j$ and $\Phi_j$ are $[0,\infty]$-valued Borel functions on $T$.

