body:
[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] Assume $\beta>3$. Given $\varepsilon \in (0, \beta-3)$, there exists $\uc{c:correlation_decay_gf}>0$ such that, for all $n \in \N$, if $A$ and $B$ are events supported in $B(0, 3n)$ and $B(0, 4n)^{c}$, respectively, then
    \begin{equation}
        \Cov_{\lambda} \big( \textnormal{\textbf{1}}_{A}, \textnormal{\textbf{1}}_{B}) \leq \uc{c:correlation_decay_gf} n^{-\beta+3+\varepsilon}.
    \end{equation}
    In particular,~\eqref{h4} is satisfied if $\beta> 3$.

