body:
[Prop p.GMC of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Take $\gamma \in [0,2)$. The random measure $M^{\gamma}(\Gamma_{2^{-n}},dx)$ converges almost surely to a non-trivial random measure $M^{\gamma}(\Gamma,dx)$. Furthermore, for any bounded deterministic function $f$
   \begin{align*}
\int f(x) M^{\gamma}(\Gamma_{2^{-n}},dx) \to \int f(x)M^{\gamma}(\Gamma,dx),
   \end{align*}
   where the convergence is in $L^1$. Finally, there exists a sequence of measures $(M^\gamma_{\varepsilon_0}(\Gamma))_{\varepsilon_0}$ such that $M^\gamma_{\varepsilon_0}(\Gamma) \nearrow M^\gamma(\Gamma)$ as $\varepsilon_0 \searrow 0$, and that for all $\varepsilon_0>0$
   \begin{align*}
\mathbb E\left[\iint \frac{1 }{\|x-y\|^{\alpha} } M^\gamma_{\varepsilon_0}(\Gamma, dx)M^\gamma_{\varepsilon_0}(\Gamma,dy) \right]<\infty ,
   \end{align*}
   for all $\alpha\in (0,2-\gamma^2/2)$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] For $0\le p<(4a-1)/4a$, we have
\begin{equation}
	\lim_{n\to \infty}\frac{\langle N\rangle_n}{n}=\Big(\frac{a-1}{2a(1-p)-1}\Big)^2\ \ \text{a.s.}
\end{equation}
and for $p=(4a-1)/4a$, we have
\begin{equation}
	\lim_{n\to \infty}\frac{\langle N\rangle_n}{n}=4(a-1)^2\ \ \text{a.s.}
\end{equation}

