[Theorem thm:spectral_u_s of arXiv:2605.00657, 'Spectral Duality and Reset-Neutral Distributions\\ in Random Walks with Multi-Site Geometr'] For any $z\in\{1,\dots,a-1\}$ and $gamma\in(0,1)$:
\begin{align}
u(z) &= \sum_{nu=1}^{a-1} A_nu(z)\,f_nu(gamma),
\\
s(z) &= \sum_{nu=1}^{a-1} \bigl[A_nu(z)+B_nu(z)\bigr]\,f_nu(gamma),

\end{align}
where the spectral coefficients are
\begin{align}
A_nu(z) &= \frac{2}{a}\left(\frac{q}{p}\right)^{z/2}
\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu z}{a}\right)\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu}{a}\right),
\\
B_nu(z) &= \frac{2}{a}\left(\frac{p}{q}\right)^{(a-z)/2}
\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu(a-z)}{a}\right)\sin\!\left(\frac{pinu}{a}\right),

\end{align}
and the spectral transfer function is
\begin{equation}
f_nu(gamma) := \frac{\lambda_nu(1-gamma)}{1-\lambda_nu(1-gamma)}.

\end{equation}

[Theorem thm:ber-auc:bound:auc:bernstein of arXiv:2609.02304, 'Bayes-Optimal BER and AUC: \\Estimation and Evaluation of Estimators'] For any $\delta > 0$,
  with probability at least $1 - \delta$,
  we have \IfRestatingTF{
