[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2608.05679, 'Small ball probabilities and Chung's law of the iterated logarithm for Gaussian Volterra p'] Assume that Condition \eqref{eq constant cond} holds. Then, for every $t> s\ge0$,
\begin{align}
\operatorname{Var}
\left(
X(t)\mid \sigma\{X(r):\, 0\le r\le s\}
\right)
\geq
c_{2,1}t^{2\alpha+2\beta}|t-s|^{2\gamma+3},
\end{align}
where $\operatorname{Var}(X(t)\mid\sigma\{X(r):r\le s\})$ denotes the
conditional variance of $X(t)$ given the $\sigma$-algebra generated by
$\{X(r):r\le s\}$.

