[Proposition prop:Jx of arXiv:2604.10214, 'Large deviations for maximum local time of simple random walk in dimensions \texorpdfstrin'] There exists a constant \(M=M(\beta_1,\beta_2)\in\mathbb N^+\) such that
\begin{align}
\mathbb Q\Bigl(\sup_{x\in\mathbb Z^d}\#\mathcal J_x\le M\Bigr)=1-o(1).
\end{align}

