[Lemma lem:SausageIntersection of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] There exist a constant $c, C_2 > 0$, depending only on $d$, $m$, and $C$, such that for all $\eta, e_+ \in \mathrm{Centre}(C)$ with $\left\lVert\eta - e_+\right\rVert_1 = i \ne 0$, we have
    \begin{equation}

        \abs{\left\{\zeta \in B_1(r,\eta) \, \colon \, e_+ \in S(\eta,\zeta)\right\}} \leqslant C_2i \cdot \max \set{1, \brac{\frac{r}{i}}^{(d-1)(m-1)}}
    \end{equation}
    for all $r \in \mathbb{N}$ with $r \leqslant cn$, and $n$ large enough.

