body:
[Theorem theorem_localized_eigenvector_localization of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under (main_assm of the paper), given any $k\in[\![{1,DN}]\!]$, suppose there exists a positive constant $\varepsilon_A$ such that
\begin{equation}
\|A\|_{\text{\rm{HS}}}\le N^{1/3-\varepsilon_A}{\mathfrak{r}}\left({k}\right)^{-1/3} . 
\end{equation}
Then, for any small constant $\varepsilon\in(0,2{\varepsilon}_A)$, there exists a constant $\varepsilon_0=\varepsilon_0\left({\varepsilon}\right)>0$ such that
\begin{equation}\nonumber
    \begin{aligned}
        \mathbb P\left(\max_{a=1}^D \|E_a{\bf v}_k\|^2 \le 1 - N^{-2/3+\varepsilon}{\mathfrak{r}}\left({k}\right)^{2/3}\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^2\right)\le N^{-\varepsilon_0}.
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
As a consequence, it implies that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P\left(\max_{a=1}^D \|E_a{\bf v}_k\|^2 \le 1 - N^{-c}\right)\le N^{-c}
\end{equation}
for a constant $c>0$ depending on ${\varepsilon}_A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

