body:
[Definition def_balanced of arXiv:2507.06522, 'Balanced multi-species spin glasses'] We say the multi-species parameter pair $(\vc\Delta,\vc\lambda)$ is \textit{balanced} if
\begin{equation}  \tag{H3} 
\begin{split}
\Delta^2_{t} \quad &\text{does not depend on $t\in\mathscr{S}$ for $p=1$, and} \\
\sum_{s_2,\dots,s_p\in\mathscr{S}}\Delta^2_{t,s_2,\dots,s_p}\lambda_{s_2}\cdots\lambda_{s_p} \quad &\text{does not depend on $t\in\mathscr{S}$, for every $p\geqslant2$.}
\end{split}
\end{equation}

[Lemma minimizer z=1, uninformative of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] If
    \begin{equation}
        \mathsf{SNR}\rbr{\lambda,B}=\sigma_{\max}\rbr{\Diag\rbr{\sqrt{\lambda}}\rbr{B\odot B}\Diag\rbr{\sqrt{\lambda}}}<1,
    \end{equation}
    then $\chi^\ast(1)=-\mathbf{1}_L$ is a strict local minimizer of $\cR(\cdot,1)$ and satisfies~(equation eq:first and strict second order condition of the paper).

