body:
[Theorem 7 (Worst-direction gap under balanced projective separation) of arXiv:2608.26877, 'When Is the Sharp Covariance Envelope Tight? Feature-Only Geometry for Volume-Sampled Leas'] Let
\begin{equation}
 \sigma_0=\frac{\sqrt{39}}8.
\end{equation}
For every $d=4^n$, $n\geq1$, and every integer $1\leq r<d/2$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \frac{3r}{38(d-1)}
 \leq\Delta^*_{d,r}(\sigma_0)
 <\frac r{d-r}.}

\end{equation}
The lower inequality is uniform over every design in
$\mathcal C_d(\sigma_0)$ and every fixed response in the domain
$L^*(A,y)>0$.  The strict upper inequality is supplied by the single
design-response pair in Proposition~\ref{app:bg:prop:witness}.

