[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2609.03243, 'Weighted Ces\`aro type operators on the weighted Bergman spaces in the unit ball'] Let $\alpha>-1$, $\beta>0$ and $\mu$ be a positive Borel measure on $[0,1)$. Then $\mathcal C_{\mu,\beta}^{\xi}: H^{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_n)\to H^{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_n)$ is bounded if and only if 
\begin{equation}
    \int_{[0,1)}\frac{{\rm d}\mu(t)}{(1-t)^{\beta}}<\infty.
\end{equation}

