[Lemma 45 (Mild Variation of Constants) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumption \ref{ass:regular_obstacles} hold. For any penalization parameter $\varepsilon > 0$ and any initial state $(t, x) \in [0, T] \times H$, the continuous obstacle $\Phi$ satisfies the following identity:
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
    \Phi(t, x) &= e^{-\frac{T-t}{\varepsilon}} P_{t,T}[\Phi(T, \cdot)](x) + \int_t^T e^{-\frac{s-t}{\varepsilon}} P_{t,s} \Big[ -\partial_s \Phi(s, \cdot) - \langle \cdot, A^* \nabla \Phi(s, \cdot) \rangle_H \\
    & \quad- \langle b(s, \cdot), \nabla \Phi(s, \cdot) \rangle_H - \frac{1}{2} \Tr \big( \sigma(s, \cdot) \sigma^*(s, \cdot) \nabla^2 \Phi(s, \cdot) \big) + \frac{1}{\varepsilon} \Phi(s, \cdot) \Big](x) \, \mathrm{d}s.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

