[Thm 7 of arXiv:2609.00758, 'Deformations of Compact Calabi--Yau and Fano Varieties with Isolated Singularities'] Let $X$ be as in Theorem \ref{thm: CY1}. Denote by $X^\reg\sb X$ the regular locus and suppose that
\begin{equation}
\text{the connecting homomorphism $H^n(X^\reg,\C)\to H^{n+1}(X,X^\reg;\C)$ is surjective.}
\end{equation}
Then there exist a semi-universal deformation $f:\cX\to\Def(X)$ and a Zariski dense open subset $\De\sb \Def(X)$ such that for every $t\in\De$ the singularities of $f^{-1}(t)$ have $b^{1,n-2}=l^{1,n-2}=0.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$, $f:\cube^n\to [-1,1]$, and $p\in [1,2]$,
\begin{equation}
    \left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^p}^{p} \geq C^{\text{\rm\ref{thm:high-order-Poincare-type-Boolean}}}(p)^k\Wop^{\geq k}(f),
\end{equation}
with $C^{\text{\rm\ref{thm:high-order-Poincare-type-Boolean}}}(p)=2^{1-p}/\Beta(\frac{1}{2};\frac{p}{2},\frac{p}{2})$, where $\Beta(x;a,b) := \int_0^x t^{a-1} \left(1-t\right)^{b-1} \dif t$ is the incomplete Beta function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

