[Lemma Greydis of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] We keep the previous notation. We assume $\mathbf{A1}$--$\mathbf{A4}$. For all $z\! \in \!  [0, a_p]$, we set $\psi_p (z) \! :=\! b_p \big( \varphi_{\xi_p} \big(1\! -\! \frac{1}{a_p}z \big) \! -\! 1 + \frac{1}{a_p}z\big)$, where we set $b_p\!:=a_pc_p$. Then $b_p\rightarrow\infty$, and the laws of $(\mathtt{Ht}_{ p})_{p\in \mathbb{N}}$ are tight on $\mathbb{R}_+$ iff the following condition is satisfied: \vspace{-0.1cm}
\begin{equation}

\lim_{z\to \infty} \limsup_{p\to \infty} \int_{z}^{a_p}\!\!  \frac{du}{\psi_p(u)}= 0 \; .
\end{equation} 
In that case, the Grey condition ((Grey of the paper)) is satisfied, $\mathtt{Ext}$ is a.s.~finite and $\mathtt{Ht}_{ p} \! \to \! \mathtt{Ext}$ in law on $\mathbb{R}_+$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 75 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] There exist  $d_{0}\in(1,d)$ and a constant    $N $, depending only
on $d,\delta$, 
 such that for any ($\lambda\geq\varkappa_{0}^{2}\rho_{b}^{-2}$)  ball  $B$ of radius $\rho\leq \varkappa_{0}/(2\sqrt\lambda)$ 
 and $p\geq d_{0}  $, we have
\begin{equation}

\| g_{\cA}\|_{L_{p/(p-1)}(B)}\leq N \rho^{-d /p }
\| g_{\cA}\|_{L_{1}(2B )} , 
\end{equation}
which is equivalently rewritten as
$$
\Big(\dashint_{B}g^{p/(p-1)}_{\cA}\,dx \Big)^{(p-1)/p}
\leq N\dashint_{2B }g_{\cA}\,dx.
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

