[Lemma asymp_uniforme of arXiv:2411.02156, 'Martin boundary of a degenerate Reflected Brownian Motion in a wedge'] Let $\alpha^* < \alpha_1 < \alpha^{**}$ and $\epsilon > 0$. Then, there exist constants $\eta > 0$ and $r_0 >0$ such that
\begin{equation}
h_\alpha(r\cos(\alpha_1), r\sin(\alpha_1)) \geq \frac{1}{2}e^{r(x(\alpha_1)\cos(\alpha_1) + y(\alpha_1)\sin(\alpha_1) - \epsilon)}
\end{equation}
for all $r \geq r_0$ and $\alpha \in [\alpha_1-\eta, \alpha_1 + \eta]$.

[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2604.04848, '\bf Addendum to:\\ Bounds for survival probabilities in \\ supercritical Galton-Watson pro'] For every $r\ge2$ and every $\ze\in(0,1)$, the pgfs $\varphiNB$ and $\varphiFL$ satisfy
\begin{linenomath}\begin{equation}
	\varphiFL(x;\pNB,\rNB) \le \varphiNB\Bigl(x;r,\frac{\ze(1-\ze^r)}{1-\ze^{r+1}}\Bigr) \;\text{ for every }x\in[0,1]\,.
\end{equation}\end{linenomath}
Equality holds if and only if $x = \PinfNB$ or $x=1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

