[Proposition 37 (Lower Bound and Submartingale Property) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumptions \ref{ass:coefficients} and \ref{ass:problem_data} hold. Assume that the obstacle $\Phi$ is admissible in the sense of Definition \ref{def:admissible_obstacle}. Let $V$ be the exact mild solution to the parabolic variational inequality in the sense of Definition \ref{def:mild_subsolutions}. For any initial state $(t, x) \in [0, T] \times H$ and any admissible stopping time $\tau \in \mathcal{T}_{t, T}$, the expected cost functional $J$ defined in \eqref{eq:def_cost} satisfies:
\begin{equation}
    V(t, x) \le J(t, x; \tau).
\end{equation}

