body:
[Lemma lem:complex of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] Suppose that $\varphi$ is an analytic function in the strip $\{\xi:|\mathrm{Im}(\xi)| < \pi/4 \}$ with a  zero of order $D$ at $\xi=0$,  such that $\sup_{\xi : |\mathrm{Im}(\xi)| < \pi/4} |\varphi(\xi)| \le 1$.
 Then for any $\xi \in \mathbb R$, it holds that
\begin{align}
     |\varphi(\xi)| \le \tanh(|\xi|)^D  . 
\end{align}

