[Lemma lem:girsanov of arXiv:2605.26652, 'Pathological Large Deviations of the KMP Process in Dimension $d\ge 2$'] Under the probability measures $\mathbb{Q}^{N,K}$ given by (equation eq:RND-tilt-3 of the paper), the processes $\xi^N_t$ are Markov with generator given by \begin{equation}
{\mathcal L_t^{N,H,K} = N^2\sum_{x\sim y} L^{H,K}_{x,y,t};}
\end{equation} \begin{equation}
{L^{H,K}_{x,y,t}F(\xi)
=\int_0^1 r_t(x,y,p,\xi)\big[F(\xi^{x,y,p})-F(\xi)\big] \,\mathrm d p.}
\end{equation} Moreover, under $\mathbb{Q}^{N,K}$, the empirical jump measure $\mu^N$ has predictable intensity
\[
{N^2 r_t(x,y,p,\xi^N_{t-})\,\mathrm d p\,\mathrm d t,}
\]
and the initial condition is distributed $$\xi^N_0\sim \nu^N_{u_0, a} $$ as a slowly varying local equilibrium with mass conditioned not to exceed $a$, as in Lemma (lem:svle of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2512.04544, 'On the diameter of random uniform hypergraphs in dense regime'] Let $t,c,d,n,p$ and  $N$ be as in Assumption \ref{ass main} and $\delta_1$  be as in \Cref{lemma 14}. Let $1 \leq k \leq d -1$ and $ v \in  \Gamma_{k-1} (x) $ be a fixed vertex. 
Suppose 
\[
c_k={ n- \vert N_{k-1}(x) \vert\choose t- 1}p.
\]
Then, for large $n$, we have 
\begin{align}
&\Prob(|H_k^1(x,v)-c_k|>\delta_1c_k\given \Omega_{k,x})\le 2 n^ { - 12 } \mbox{ and }
\\& \Prob(\vert H_k^{1,0} (x,v) \vert\ge  (1- \delta_1 )c_k-10\given \Omega_{k,x})\ge 1-  \frac{ 4(t-1)^{11} }{n^{11} } .
\end{align}
